{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread","id":1444431,"title":"[V5] The Lasombra thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-17T19:36:56-07:00","id":1444431,"title":"[V5] The Lasombra thread","content":"The thread for discussing all things Keeper.<br /> <br /> Oblivion vs. Obternation<br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla<br /> <br /> The remaining Lasombra back in the Sabbat<br /> <br /> Their new weakness<br /> <br /> How SHOULD the Lasombra have been updated<br /> <br /> Also, did Talley really kill Lucita or shall she be Regent?<br /> <br /> Here ya go!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:09:04-07:00","id":1444437,"title":"","content":"I am mostly indifferent to the change of Obternation to Oblivion. It feels a bit random, but not enough so to be an issue.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of at least some of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla. The old segregations of the game (such as no Lasombra, Tzimisce or Giovanni among the Anarchs, no Tzimisce among the Camarilla, and so on) always felt counterintuitive to me, a bit of social rules imposed on the setting which did not reflect real human behavior. That some Lasombra would decide the Sabbat is a disaster and want to jump ship makes perfect sense in a &quot;one step back, two steps forward&quot; kind of way. And it opens game possibilities for players.<br /> <br /> Of course some Lasombra will stay with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> All the clans have been rewritten in ways small and large in V5. The changes to the Lasombra are simply part of that.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with how they have been updated.<br /> <br /> Talley did not kill my raven-haired dark angel... I mean, Talley did not kill Lucita because that would be a waste of a good character. And she will probably be a leader of one of the Sabbat factions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:43:15-07:00","id":1444442,"title":"","content":"Well. From reading the Chicago: By Night book I never got the impression that the Lasombra joined the Camarilla per se. Some did. The short adventure at the end of the book kinda makes the PCs convince the Prince to go through with it, and he is giving the Lasombra quite a harsh tax to pay. And this is only Chicago, we don't know if other princes agreed. The Lasombra in Chicago feels more like refugees than anything else. I mean, even if the Lasombra is the ones who wish to join, we don't know how other Camarilla elders reacted to it, and if there's a consensus about it. We only know that Kevin Jackson agreed (as far as I know).<br /> <br /> I think that we won't really know until we will get the Sabbat book. As much as I liked Chicago: By Night, it is nothing but a flavor book IMO, and the canon there is very sketchy, werewolves are being killed there like they were fledgling vampires, I mean the prince killed the alpha of a pack with a decorative sword he took down from a wall. Or the fact that one Nosferatu is impersonating another Nosferatu and no other elder with auspex apparently notices it.<br /> <br /> About Oblivion. It should have been its own thing. I liked it when I didn't know what was the darkness that the Lasombra summon exactly, tieing it to Necromancy kinda steal all the mystery. I think game-wise the powers are different enough to warrant their own disciplines, and I think that it is very confusing for new players who don't understand the lore, kinda muddy the water with regard to the specialties of the clans who use Oblivion. I would really prefer it if Necromancy was part of Blood Sorcery, because, in a way, it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T00:39:24-07:00","id":1444458,"title":"","content":"I have thought of two possibly interesting stories involving a Lasombra - <br /> <br /> 1. Two recent emigres have arrived in the city about the same time: a warrior assamite, and a lasombra. The Prince has decreed that both shall serve his court as Scourge for the remainder of the year. At the end of that time, the one whose performance has pleased him best will be allowed to stay, and the other must find haven elsewhere. Both of the dangerous new arrivals have made it clear they intend to win the contest. Now the Domain's Caitiff and Anarchs have serious reason to be afraid.... <br /> <br /> 2. The relatively young Ventrue Prince of a Western American city has been caught <i>en flagrante delicto</i> with his Lasombra Scourge. The two vampires have formed a mutual blood bond, an act disparaged within the Camarilla as perversion. The region's Ventrue Elders are outraged, and clamor for the Prince to be removed for this violation of <i>dignitas</i>. The Primogen however, are divided--some continue to support the Prince, while others consider the opportunity to place their own puppet on the throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:09:31-07:00","id":1444464,"title":"","content":"..Haven't we already had one of these from you?<br /> <br /> First thing the new lasombra weakness is uncharacteristically emasculating for one of the most man's-man* clans out there. How can a clan known for their agression, fierce individualism and self-made bosses be lowered to have a ghoul take their phone calls for them? How can a clan known to trust no-one not even their reflections come to put so much faith into a retainer? compounded by the fact that this weakness is just so... modern. Vampire's are meant to be unchanging immortals, not fellows who go through version updates every few decades; not being captured by technology would mean they had virtually no weakness before the later modern era. It just feels like someone completely missunderstands the lasombra, or they perfectly understand the lasombra and hate them and want to change them to be more nice or something outrageous like that.<br /> <br /> *Yes, the Lasombra have women, and they're excellent, goal oriented monsters who enjoy stepping on people.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are gone, and as for the Lasombra joining the Camarilla.. again, this just feels like an attempt of emasculation. They've gone from kings of the night to wipping boys at the bottom of the rung in the declining camarilla. Did they come dressed in Gimp suits? When did such an S clan become a purely M clan? The part that doesn't feel like it's an emasculation is the part where the Cam is now openly religious and that somewhat ties into the Lasombra being the posterboys for religious vampires... but the removal of a secular camarilla is also something I don't like, with the &quot;heroic&quot; Brujah being replaced by notably catholic authoritarians it just seems like the Cam have become an idealistic left-wing imagining of republicans (who, if we're being honest, should probably be keeping the Brujah)<br /> <br /> <br /> How should the Lasombra have been updated?<br /> Barely.<br /> You could just have a few more defects and have the Magisters embrace a few more children and apply for a council seat. You don't need to give the clan an idiot ball and have them defect en mass to a dying cam with so many restrictions where the anarchs are very much open and aren't going to bust balls for members. You should also consider that defections are going to be done on a local level and it's rather absurd to have some rules for international defections.<br /> <br /> Also Obtenebration could've used a slight nerf. Oblivion is unwarranted overkill and really messes the clan's identity with the old Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:38:34-07:00","id":1444468,"title":"","content":"Replying from the other thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1369651-should-kuei-jin-be-in-v5?p=1444457#post1444457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should know the US literally did that to Nazis and to a lesser extent (but more shockingly) Japanese war criminals (who asked for amnesty in exchange for the results of brutal human experimentation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of Operation Paperclip and the like. The thing is those largely happened after the Axis powers had surrendered and WW2 was essentially over. They very much weren't recruiting members of Nazi Germany and Japan's elite in the middle of the war and immediately handing vast amounts of economic, military and political power over to them while the war was still progressing. Those who did become turncoats while the war was ongoing were watched very carefully and weren't given the benefit of full trust.<br /> <br /> Unlike with WW2, the Sabbat never surrendered or gave up. They're still at war with the Camarilla, and a number of these Lasombra who joined the Camarilla are old and have spent decades, if not centuries at war with the Camarilla. So I would expect the Camarilla to be keeping a very weary eye on them, not just freely and immediately handing them the levers of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:48:28-07:00","id":1444470,"title":"","content":"the lasombra are a great example on what's wrong with V5, fine ideas horrible execution.<br /> <br /> the lasombra joining the camarilla is a fine idea, but the deal they took for joining boggles the mind how any writer could think this was in any way rational. the lasombra have no reason to join the cam (they have a reason to leave the sabbath, not join the cam) the deal they got was incredibly harsh, for lasombra that held certain ranks in the sabbath you could justify it but for your average pack priest, grunt or something of that caliber? no way in hell.<br /> <br /> oblivion is also horribly executed, obtenebration and necromancy are just too different, at least with the new protean and blood magic there's some slim justification why they're one discipline oblivion doesn't, it just doesn't have a uniting aspect outside of flavour text, the real kicker is that they did try to give it some overarching aspect in the disciplines themselves but honestly who thinks stains on crit rouse is a good mechanic, it's tacked on with zero integration into the discipline itself and it further confuses what the fuck humanity is supposed to be, further more the stains aren't earned like every other way you can gain stains. every other way you can gain stains are due to decisions and/or actions taken in character, not due to a bad dice roll, just so they can pretend to add gravity to a mechanic that doesn't have it.<br /> <br /> the worst part to me is that all these issues could be fixed with just a rewrite, an extensive rewrite perhaps but that's all it needed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 04-18-2021, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:56:45-07:00","id":1444473,"title":"","content":"Issue is vampires tend to operate on an individual or city-state level rather than on a sect level. It doesn't matter that Terry of the Sabbat has been quite successsful in attacking the Camarilla city of Dalas, Texas, it matters that he hasn't offended anyone in the Camarilla city of Austin, Texas, where he plans to join, and should nobody between the cities have a sufficiently close relationship where calls for vengance can be made... Terry should be just fine. Now if Terry, who's spent his unlife near the border, were to try his luck somewhere far away, it would be even less of a concern. <br /> <br /> In reality, most defections are going to be done through prestation. Because literally all sects honour prestation regardless of which sect it's coming from, bar perhaps the Anarchs who're 50% fledglings and don't know how serious older vampires take these things. All you gotta do is play around a bit with foreign debt, then use your credit score to have someone vouch for you in another city, and you're good to go (provided you don't get caught). Just ariving and saying you'll be the prince's bitch-boy is suicidal, because the prince has no reason to trust you would only take you if he's desperate. A universal camarilla decree that Lasombra can join the cam after headhunting is just a comedy of errors that proves nothing but the incompetence of Lasombra in foreign relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T03:10:44-07:00","id":1444477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444470#post1444470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the lasombra are a great example on what's wrong with V5, fine ideas horrible execution.<br /> <br /> the lasombra joining the camarilla is a fine idea, but the deal they took for joining boggles the mind how any writer could think this was in any way rational. the lasombra have no reason to join the cam (they have a reason to leave the sabbath, not join the cam) the deal they got was incredibly harsh, for lasombra that held certain ranks in the sabbath you could justify it but for your average pack priest, grunt or something of that caliber? no way in hell.<br /> <br /> oblivion is also horribly executed, obtenebration and necromancy are just too different, at least with the new protean and blood magic there's some slim justification why they're one discipline oblivion doesn't, it just doesn't have a uniting aspect outside of flavour text, the real kicker is that they did try to give it some overarching aspect in the disciplines themselves but honestly who thinks stains on crit rouse is a good mechanic, it's tacked on with zero integration into the discipline itself and it further confuses what the fuck humanity is supposed to be, further more the stains aren't earned like every other way you can gain stains. every other way you can gain stains are due to decisions and/or actions taken in character, not due to a bad dice roll, just so they can pretend to add gravity to a mechanic that doesn't have it.<br /> <br /> the worst part to me is that all these issues could be fixed with just one rewrite, that's all it needed</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume that you are talking about the thing that they need to pay with their elders right? I understand that it was only Kevin Jackson's idea in Chicago. Not the entire Camarilla policy. At list, this is what the book is suggesting. I assume that every prince will have their own say about it, and some might even not allow it. It's not that Kevin was contacted by higher-ups in the Camarilla's hierarchy that gave him orders to allow the Lasomba into Chicago. He was asked directly by the Lasombra and made the decision by himself.<br /> <br /> This is why I am not entirely sure that the Lasombra really joined the Camarilla, it's more like they joined Kevin's court in Chicago, and it might be a precedent in more cities, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T03:28:07-07:00","id":1444479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444473#post1444473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Issue is vampires tend to operate on an individual or city-state level rather than on a sect level. </div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's kind of where I'm getting stuck. Just because the Inner Circle said these guys are all trustworthy, I have a hard time imagining most vampires would just nod and accept it and go along with it. I'd assume the reaction from most would be skepticism, at best, and any Lasombra would be expected to spend quite a bit of time (in the vampiric sense) proving that they can be trusted with political power and authority and that this isn't an elaborate ruse to infiltrate and undermine the city to turn it over to the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> That's also something I expect would happen at some point, because surely you'll have some Lasombra decide they were happier being the masters of the Sabbat and that if maybe by handing the Sabbat the keys to the inner workings of a city's Camarilla they'll be able to get back in. And that'll be a black mark against all the Lasombra. They'd really better be careful to police their own.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, I imagine for most vampires their response will be something like, &quot;I don't care if the Inner Council says these defectors proved they're all trustworthy, they're going to need to prove to me and everyone in this city that they can be trusted.&quot; And given vampiric lifespans that's probably going take take more than just a year or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-18-2021, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T04:03:21-07:00","id":1444482,"title":"","content":"The weakness seems way harsh and punishing for one of the clans most likely to compete for control over corporations and high society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T04:12:29-07:00","id":1444483,"title":"","content":"Weaknesses exist to encourage vampires to work towards their strengths and style of play (and also because shared weakness brings people together and turns competitors into clans). The new lasombra weakness is backwards because it discourages you from playing lasombra the way you are meant to; Potence means you get your hands dirty and can do things yourself, Dominate means you are authpritative and boss folks around.. screwing over your ability to communicate is the last weakness you should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T04:32:31-07:00","id":1444484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444483#post1444483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaknesses exist to encourage vampires to work towards their strengths and style of play (and also because shared weakness brings people together and turns competitors into clans). The new lasombra weakness is backwards because it discourages you from playing lasombra the way you are meant to; Potence means you get your hands dirty and can do things yourself, Dominate means you are authpritative and boss folks around.. screwing over your ability to communicate is the last weakness you should have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu live in the sewers because their weakness and powers push them towards a life hidden from humanity, and into territories which have access to numerous animals and tunnels.<br /> <br /> Gangrel wander the wilds because their weakness also pushes them towards avoiding cameras while their powers give them supreme mobility in territories where they face very little competition from other vampires.<br /> <br /> Ventrue have both the greatest need for a safe, stable herd, and the greatest ability to gain a herd, so of course they focus on the centers of power and encourage peace and order.<br /> <br /> Brujah have great ability to gain a herd, but they need chaos to hide their routine rages, as they don't have the direct ability to hide from human eyes that the Nos and Gangrel do. So they hide in violent subcultures.<br /> <br /> You can pretty much go down the line and see how the combination of their strengths and weaknesses pushes each clan into behaving in a so-called &quot;stereotypical&quot; way.<br /> <br /> Everyone except the Lasombra. They now have a weakness that frankly would work better as an alternate universe version of the Gangrel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T04:54:23-07:00","id":1444485,"title":"","content":"regarding the new bane i don't see the issue. the way i see it the old lasombra bane created 2 issues it made them easier to identify as a vampire (just check their reflection) and made them dependent on ghouls for their looks. the new bane seems to just do the same thing it just applies to technology as well as mirrors<br /> <br /> so could antbody explain where my logic falls apart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 04-18-2021, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:10:03-07:00","id":1444486,"title":"","content":"The old lasombra weakness largely served to make them paranoid, contolling, and distinguishable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:22:53-07:00","id":1444487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444486#post1444486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old lasombra weakness largely served to make them paranoid, contolling, and distinguishable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I thought it made them prone to having stylists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:23:27-07:00","id":1444488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444486#post1444486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old lasombra weakness largely served to make them paranoid, contolling, and distinguishable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> could you elaborate as to how the old flaw did that and why the new one fails to do so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:32:05-07:00","id":1444490,"title":"","content":"For example, as a Lasombra, to avoid being spotted for not having a reflection, I might be inclined to avoid busy streets or ones with large windows, I will want to stay indoors all night due to a rain increasing the amount pf reflective surfaces, only visit a club that i control or have vetted for few mirrors. My choices for vehicle are greatly limited, so i need to make sure I have my own system for emergency transport. Every time someone whips out a mirror to check their makeup or tries to look behind them in a car i need to act. I would likely need to push my no mirror agenda for salloons or elysium. It all just pushes me towards becoming a paranoid control freak, with a decisive all or nothing approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:36:53-07:00","id":1444491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444484#post1444484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone except the Lasombra. They now have a weakness that frankly would work better as an alternate universe version of the Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in this vein (pardon the pun), let\u2019s throw that bane away away and even prior editions\u2019 \u201cno reflections\u201d (mirrors and surfaces smooth enough for clear reflections didn\u2019t become common until relatively late in human development... so while a stereotypical bit of vampire lore, it wouldn\u2019t be a significant weakness until many centuries after it was laid upon them; reflections are also less apparent at night).<br /> <br /> Say you\u2019re building the Lasombra from scratch. What would make a good bane/weakness that fits them and their disciplines that would work for them in the way the Nos, Gangrel, Ventrue and Brujah\u2019s inform their overall styles?<br /> <br /> Honestly? My first inclination if I were devising them from scratch would be to give them the clan flaw similar to the True Brujah. Their ability to empathize with others is as cold as the night they command. They are imperious rulers who use strength (potence), will (dominate) and fear (obtenabration) without an ounce of pity within them. So a penalty to all social rolls involving empathy or compassion.<br /> <br /> It would be a real flaw throughout every age, encourange their distance from \u201crabble\u201d and why they are so utterly imperious and intolerant of weakness/failure.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s just one thought... what are yours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:43:21-07:00","id":1444493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444490#post1444490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, as a Lasombra, to avoid being spotted for not having a reflection, I might be inclined to avoid busy streets or ones with large windows, I will want to stay indoors all night due to a rain increasing the amount pf reflective surfaces, only visit a club that i control or have vetted for few mirrors. My choices for vehicle are greatly limited, so i need to make sure I have my own system for emergency transport. Every time someone whips out a mirror to check their makeup or tries to look behind them in a car i need to act. I would likely need to push my no mirror agenda for salloons or elysium. It all just pushes me towards becoming a paranoid control freak, with a decisive all or nothing approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Lasombra ever showed that kind of fear of humans and in fact would have a clan culture of the exact opposite. They would be encourage to display utter indifference to the concerns of &quot;lesser beings.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:59:34-07:00","id":1444495,"title":"","content":"My Lasombra thoughts?<br /> <br /> 1. Honestly, I'm not a big fan of the new weakness. I think the Lasombra having a weakness with technology comes out of left field and frankly is a ridiculously crippling flaw in the Modern World. Harry Dresden is very hard to believe having it in the Modern World, let alone one of the most powerful Clans. Its so ubiquotous that I don't think that it matches other Clan Flaws but overwhelming is worse than the others even as they dialed down the Nosferatu, Ventrue, and Malkavian weaknesses.<br /> <br /> This is adding the mirror distortion thing on top of it that is a classic weakness of the undead. I feel like keeping the Mirror weakness and adjusting it while leaving Lasombra able to be recorded is something they should have done. Maybe add an additional quality like making them vulnerable to silver instead. So yes, the technology weakness isn't canon in my games. A Lasombra without a sports car or limousine or supervillain lair is not a true Lasombra.<br /> <br /> 2. I think Lasombra joining the Camarilla makes a pretty good balance and the story justified it well for me with the discovery that their Antediluvian is not dead. I feel like that is the kind of thing that would utterly shake the foundations of the Clan among the highest and lowest. The highest realizing that they underestimated the kind of fight that they were taking on and the lowest getting a taste of REAL power.<br /> <br /> I made a comparison between the two &quot;Clans of Faith&quot; a long time ago with the fact that the Lasombra represent those who religion is a tool to exploit and that don't actually believe while the Setites are the fanatics who believe to the point it utterly warps their worldview. The Sabbat was never meant to be a thing Lasombra died FOR, it was a thing the Lasombra created for other suckers to die for them. So them noping the fuck out of it was something I believed in.<br /> <br /> 3. I think the Lasombra joining the Camarilla is something that they lucked out on. They would have done it over decades if there wasn't a variety of factors that kind of percipitated it happening all at once now. The Gehenna War meant that it was NOW time to make the jump for them but the Camarilla were only in a place to make it happen because the Tremere down, the Brujah were gone, the Gangrel had already left, and the Anarchs were on the rise. Plus the Beckoning meant that the Camarilla's biggest guns and smartest players were gone. In short, the Lasombra knew that now was the only time in the history of the world they could make this deal and not getting squeezed.<br /> <br /> My view on the Camarilla is they think the deals and restrictions they're making are enough to finish off the Sabbat or severely weaken it while also keeping the Lasombra at bay. I also think that they never intended to give the Lasombra a chance to gain power. However, right now the Camarilla is in a state of chaos and the Lasombra know that very Games of Throne-esque ideal.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-000541132548-j9759e-t500x500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 4. I also have the suspicion that the Lasombra's defection is percipitated by the fact that there's a lot more Lasombra who feel like the Sabbat is a money and time sink. While this is just an observation, Sierra Burrace probably is more common than most Keepers admit. A highly ambitious, very driven Neonate or Ancilla who notes that her other vampires are uninterested in mortal power or wealth despite how much their Disciplines could make them. The Sabbat takes massive amounts of your time with rituals, hunting, and more that could be used to build a personal power base. Instead, pack politics means corraling your fellow Sabbat far more than is really useful if you'd like your own drug empire or hedge fund. Even Lasombra that are forbidden from being a Primogen or Prince for sixty years (which is a rule that I imagine most Lasombra scoff at, &quot;You don't become Prince by obeying rules&quot;), that's time plenty of them would like to focus on gaining mortal influence that they've been denied.<br /> <br /> 5. Even so, I agree with the 50-50 split as a general rule. Cardinals and Archbishops aren't leaving their positions unless they can get something similar. I fully see the Sabbat Lasombra also perhaps having UNDERestimated how many of their kind would defect. One of the jokes is that Talley may have killed or tried to kill Lucita to defect only to have plenty of Lasombra trying to kill HIM to defect. Probably them targeted by their fellows. Which is what you get when you're a clan of relentless assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-18-2021, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T07:24:51-07:00","id":1444499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444468#post1444468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike with WW2, the Sabbat never surrendered or gave up. They're still at war with the Camarilla, and a number of these Lasombra who joined the Camarilla are old and have spent decades, if not centuries at war with the Camarilla. So I would expect the Camarilla to be keeping a very weary eye on them, not just freely and immediately handing them the levers of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>[mansplaining] Well, actually... the only Camarilla authority figure to accept Lasombra is Prince Jackson, who is only decades old and thus - by definition - has not been fighting the Keepers for centuries. The deal of one existing Lasombra for one destroyed Lasombra is possibly unique to his city, Chicago. Many of the old guard might reject any deals with the Lasombra out of hand and heap scorn on Jackson for making a deal. And even in Chicago its not like the Keepers are just given a position on the primogen, they just have the luxury of not being shot on sight.[/mansplaining]<br /> <br /> It is interesting to speculate on how other Camarilla cities, and the inner circle, react to Jackson's deal but at this point we do not have any official answers. The deal to accept them is unique to Chicago, at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:13:45-07:00","id":1444506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444495#post1444495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view on the Camarilla is they think the deals and restrictions they're making are enough to finish off the Sabbat or severely weaken it while also keeping the Lasombra at bay. I also think that they never intended to give the Lasombra a chance to gain power. However, right now the Camarilla is in a state of chaos and the Lasombra know that very Games of Throne-esque ideal.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-000541132548-j9759e-t500x500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One would hope the Lasombra are bright enough to not follow the advice of guy whose schemes to exploit the chaos ended with his bleeding out on the floor of the court once enough people had grown tired of his shenanigans and was no closer to the power he sought than when the story began.<br /> <br /> No, it seems to me that the Lasombra would be more likely to follow the more apt advice;<br /> <br /> \u201cPower is power.\u201d<br /> <br /> The speaker of that truth outlasted Baelish and was only done in when someone with even more power and ruthlessness showed up. So even in death she was proven correct.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-18-2021, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:14:39-07:00","id":1444507,"title":"","content":"The sabbat have lost mexico city. How much more defeated can they be? I think a lot of lasombra are probably fleeing like rats off a sinking ship. Tzimisce have picked the anarch and lasombra the camarilla. Nevertheless, i think the sabbat will rise again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:41:43-07:00","id":1444510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444499#post1444499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [mansplaining] Well, actually... the only Camarilla authority figure to accept Lasombra is Prince Jackson, who is only decades old and thus - by definition - has not been fighting the Keepers for centuries. The deal of one existing Lasombra for one destroyed Lasombra is possibly unique to his city, Chicago. Many of the old guard might reject any deals with the Lasombra out of hand and heap scorn on Jackson for making a deal. And even in Chicago its not like the Keepers are just given a position on the primogen, they just have the luxury of not being shot on sight.[/mansplaining]<br /> <br /> It is interesting to speculate on how other Camarilla cities, and the inner circle, react to Jackson's deal but at this point we do not have any official answers. The deal to accept them is unique to Chicago, at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually have a couple of canonical examples in other media:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Vannevar Thomas</b>, &quot;Prince&quot; of LA: Vannevar has accepted two Lasombra defectors from the Sabbat and has appointed them to be his Scourges. The job that he gives them is to murder Anarchs in the nastiest, ugliest, and most disturbing ways possible. He has also employed them against his own fellow Ventrue because they depend on his good graces. Being Sabbat, they see no problem with their job as Scourges. He also has appointed a former ghoul of Fiorenza, Prince of Mexico City, as his Sheriff. Except she had her Embraced as Lasombra not Ventrue.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Prince Helena Panhard</b>: The Prince of New York City is a real dick to the Keepers as while she's accepted a defector to her city and even gave her permission to sire, said Lasombra's childer is treated like absolute crap socially. They gave her a domain and a job looking over presentation while constantly ignoring her or snubbing her. Her sire, by contrast, avoids all Kindred functions and focuses on gaining mortal power while working with her fellow Lasombra on settling elsewhere. The &quot;good&quot; ending of the game has the protagonist frame the Malkavian Primogen for a screw up of the Prince and win her own seat at the table as well as the respect of the other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444506#post1444506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One would hope the Lasombra are bright enough to not follow the advice of guy whose schemes to exploit the chaos ended with his bleeding out on the floor of the court once enough people had grown tired of his shenanigans and was no closer to the power he sought than when the story began.<br /> <br /> No, it seems to me that the Lasombra would be more likely to follow the more apt advice;<br /> <br /> \u201cPower is power.\u201d<br /> <br /> The speaker of that truth outlasted Baelish and was only done in when someone with even more power and ruthlessness showed up. So even in death she was proven correct.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'd argue the Lasombra would say that Littlefinger did the greatest job that any Lasombra can do. He educated his childe into exceeding him and claiming his blood.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/3f/b8/55/3fb855e57bfd965937a0595b191f497d.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Lasombra basically have some very Sith ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-18-2021, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:42:29-07:00","id":1444511,"title":"","content":"Again, the difference between Lasombra and settite isnt a matter of liars vs true believers, It's more a matter of Order religion VS chaos religion, or accepted, legitimate, authoritative power vs an underground cult. The Lasombra also grasp towards binary systems; Gods or Demons, making themselves subservient to one extreme, while settites despise both and believe in their capability for freedom. Lasombra do this in part because they're authoritarian types who thus need hierachies and who else but God deserves the top spot, and part because exploring Abyss is going to make anyone religious. <br /> <br /> Which reminds me: The abyss is gone in V5. That's a bit shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:48:11-07:00","id":1444512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444511#post1444511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the difference between Lasombra and settite isnt a matter of liars vs true believers, It's more a matter of Order religion VS chaos religion, or accepted, legitimate, authoritative power vs an underground cult. The Lasombra also grasp towards binary systems; Gods or Demons, making themselves subservient to one extreme, while settites despise both and believe in their capability for freedom. Lasombra do this in part because they're authoritarian types who thus need hierachies and who else but God deserves the top spot, and part because exploring Abyss is going to make anyone religious.</div> </div> </div> </div>While my comparison is not 1:1, I tend to think it can be summarized as such:<br /> <br /> 1. The Followers of Set will die for their faith and sacrifice everything they have.<br /> 2. The Lasombra will sacrifice nothing and get others of faith to kill for them.<br /> <br /> Just my .02.<br /> <br /> I always liked Montrovant in the Grail Covenant books by my friend David Niall Wilson. Guy is a randy hedonistic Lasombra that wants the Grail to control the world's religion and keeps a monk who considers him a saint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which reminds me: The abyss is gone in V5. That's a bit shit. </div> </div> </div>This isn't something that was invented by V5. The Labyrinth/Abyss as one was established in <i>Demon: The Fallen</i> that wielded together a lot of mythologies in the World of Darkness. Which is good because it makes the Judeao-Christian themes of the Lasombra make a lot more sense as well as the infernalism of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra were always knocking on Hell's door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-18-2021, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T09:20:01-07:00","id":1444514,"title":"","content":"The Abyss in Demon was distinct from the Abyss of the Lasombra (and the Abyss near Malfeas in werewolf is also a distinct thing) Thus the Fallen being trapped under oblivion means... absolutely nothing for Lasombra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T09:21:22-07:00","id":1444515,"title":"","content":"Oi cut the spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T09:52:33-07:00","id":1444517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444515#post1444515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oi cut the spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, George R.R. Martin has said the book will end differently.<br /> <br /> Added spoiler tags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444514#post1444514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss in Demon was distinct from the Abyss of the Lasombra (and the Abyss near Malfeas in werewolf is also a distinct thing) Thus the Fallen being trapped under oblivion means... absolutely nothing for Lasombra</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not a big fan of unconnected and discontented spirituality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-18-2021, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T10:19:40-07:00","id":1444518,"title":"","content":"It's very... DnD that we'd need a shadow realm and a spirit realm and a dream realm and an even number of planes conforming to an axis of good/evil and law/chaos. The world of Darkness isn't meant to be a place with easy answers, otherwise the occult speciality would be academics rather than explicitly stating it's about knowing a large amount of BS and being able to search for a truth for that, or at the very least all the mages would get along because there's nothing much to argue about and it's very easy to know everything. Complaining about messy planes is kinda like complaining that the continents aren't neat squares. Give me some mystery, make things organic, Give me a mess. You completely undermine the Abyss mystics when you simply take their things and have them share it with everyone else. The Occult can't exist in a world where things neatly conform to your worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T10:22:34-07:00","id":1444519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444510#post1444510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We actually have a couple of canonical examples in other media...</div> </div> </div> </div>That does prove other cities and princes are taking the Lasombra, but it also says they are demanding different costs for this admission. Panhard is just being a general horses ass to them. By comparison Thomas is demanding violence and dependence. The violence Thomas's scourges are doing means they are only making enemies and the only ally they will have is Thomas himself. If he had run San Fransisco in the same way he probably would not have lost praxis.<br /> <br /> The point being, them getting into individual cities is possible if a ST allows it, and the price for admission is whatever story hook the ST develops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T10:32:55-07:00","id":1444521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444519#post1444519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does prove other cities and princes are taking the Lasombra, but it also says they are demanding different costs for this admission. Panhard is just being a general horses ass to them. By comparison Thomas is demanding violence and dependence. The violence Thomas's scourges are doing means they are only making enemies and the only ally they will have is Thomas himself. If he had run San Fransisco in the same way he probably would not have lost praxis.<br /> <br /> The point being, them getting into individual cities is possible if a ST allows it, and the price for admission is whatever story hook the ST develops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good observation.<br /> <br /> Also, the numbers of Lasombra aren't necessarily THAT huge spread among Camarilla domains. This is not a refugee crisis so to speak. At roughly 2000 vampires per Clan, barring Gehenna War losses, the Lasombra would probably have 800 defectors or so to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Making the adjustment of say, 1800 Sabbat Lasombra and 200 Lasombra Antitribu or Autakis beforehand.<br /> <br /> With hundreds of cities across the world to choose from, it's not that hard to find places for them. Especially since with those cities imposing a &quot;murder tithe&quot; that some won't make it and their numbers will go down. The actual numbers are probably less.<br /> <br /> Say, maybe 500 to 600 will make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T12:37:25-07:00","id":1444532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444518#post1444518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very... DnD that we'd need a <b>shadow realm</b> and a spirit realm and a dream realm and an even number of planes conforming to an axis of good/evil and law/chaos. The world of Darkness isn't meant to be a place with easy answers, otherwise the occult speciality would be academics rather than explicitly stating it's about knowing a large amount of BS and being able to search for a truth for that, or at the very least all the mages would get along because there's nothing much to argue about and it's very easy to know everything. Complaining about messy planes is kinda like complaining that the continents aren't neat squares. Give me some mystery, make things organic, Give me a mess. You completely undermine the Abyss mystics when you simply take their things and have them share it with everyone else. The Occult can't exist in a world where things neatly conform to your worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am not understanding, but aren't you the one who *is* arguing for the existence of a distinctive &quot;shadow realm,&quot; the Lasombra Abyss that is the source of Obtenebration and seems otherwise completely disconnected from anything else?<br /> <br /> Having the source of Lasombra shadow powers be tied up in Oblivion and the Low Umbra seems to make things less tidy and more mysterious. (Edit) I do think that the part of the Abyss/Oblivion that the Lasombra interact with should differ in some respects from other aspects, have some different rules or effects. But that doesn't necessarily mean that the line between them should be completely untraceable.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the things I like about oWoD over nWoD is that it *doesn't* try too hard to make every gamelines magical-world be a neat little box that is entirely cut off from the metaphysics of every other gameline. Obviously a Storyteller can do whatever they want at their own table, but my own readings about the Umbra recently have only reinforced the idea that the vast array of Otherworlds in the oWoD are very tangled up in one another. The Middle Umbra Near Realm Abyss might be somewhat distinct from the Abyss of the Fallen or the Labyrinth of Wraith, but there are all sorts of connections described as existing between them. The details are left up to individual Storytellers to decide, but the opportunities are laid out for you. And really, the idea that the source of power for the *undead* shadow-wielders might be associated with the Low Umbra and the manifest power of Entropy doesn't really seem like a terrible stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:02:59-07:00","id":1444629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444532#post1444532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am not understanding, but aren't you the one who *is* arguing for the existence of a distinctive &quot;shadow realm,&quot; the Lasombra Abyss that is the source of Obtenebration and seems otherwise completely disconnected from anything else?<br /> <br /> Having the source of Lasombra shadow powers be tied up in Oblivion and the Low Umbra seems to make things less tidy and more mysterious. (Edit) I do think that the part of the Abyss/Oblivion that the Lasombra interact with should differ in some respects from other aspects, have some different rules or effects. But that doesn't necessarily mean that the line between them should be completely untraceable.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the things I like about oWoD over nWoD is that it *doesn't* try too hard to make every gamelines magical-world be a neat little box that is entirely cut off from the metaphysics of every other gameline. Obviously a Storyteller can do whatever they want at their own table, but my own readings about the Umbra recently have only reinforced the idea that the vast array of Otherworlds in the oWoD are very tangled up in one another. The Middle Umbra Near Realm Abyss might be somewhat distinct from the Abyss of the Fallen or the Labyrinth of Wraith, but there are all sorts of connections described as existing between them. The details are left up to individual Storytellers to decide, but the opportunities are laid out for you. And really, the idea that the source of power for the *undead* shadow-wielders might be associated with the Low Umbra and the manifest power of Entropy doesn't really seem like a terrible stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily, it was never previously stated where Obten linked to, (it was potentially the Abyss of Wraith, or the Far Horizon of Mage/Werewolf, or something to do with the Nephandi) you could decide for your chronicle what it connected to, or if it was something totally other than all of those (the abyss between stars, the endless Hunger of Lasombra itself....something Cthonic and Mythos related). That ambiguity is gone now, it seems all darkness related stuff comes from the single source of the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:51:08-07:00","id":1444635,"title":"","content":"The mystics never knew for sure, and that was a big deal. Speculations ranged from a primordial realm outside and opposed to God's creation all the way to being sourced by something lilith grew in a garden. You were free to breath deep from the crack pipe and come up with the most batshit insane profound mystery for your mystic character to base her whole worldview around, and it was glorious. As the GM you could make whatever dramatic reveal you liked to suit your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-19-2021, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:55:02-07:00","id":1444671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444629#post1444629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not necessarily, it was never previously stated where Obten linked to, (it was potentially the Abyss of Wraith, or the Far Horizon of Mage/Werewolf, or something to do with the Nephandi) you could decide for your chronicle what it connected to, or if it was something totally other than all of those (the abyss between stars, the endless Hunger of Lasombra itself....something Cthonic and Mythos related). That ambiguity is gone now, it seems all darkness related stuff comes from the single source of the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it removes some ambiguity around Abyss Mysticism, to the extent that there is a hard 'canon' answer about something that was previously implied but not set down for sure. But for me, that connection is not especially surprising, and doesn't necessarily preclude their being a ton of distinctive properties and remaining mysteries and questions about the Lasombra Abyss that don't make it identical to other Dark Umbral phenomena. Locking down that one particular thing just doesn't ruin the whole mystery for me. I don't know enough about the crunch of V5 to know how much work might be necessary mechanically, but from a fluff standpoint I also don't see anything wrong with individual Storytellers deciding that the nature of the Abyss actually does differ from the 'canon' answer. Maybe the Abyss is a Zone, with close ties to Oblivion but plenty of other properties and metaphysical entanglements with other Realms? <br /> <br /> Also, not all &quot;darkness related stuff&quot; comes from the Abyss. There are two other Near Umbras plus the Deep Umbra that are all capable of producing darkness-related stuff. Maybe in Vampire everything is getting relegated to Oblivion/the Dark Umbra, but again, I don't see that as super concerning when we're talking about the Undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:17:53-07:00","id":1444681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444671#post1444671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that it removes some ambiguity around Abyss Mysticism, to the extent that there is a hard 'canon' answer about something that was previously implied but not set down for sure. But for me, that connection is not especially surprising, and doesn't necessarily preclude their being a ton of distinctive properties and remaining mysteries and questions about the Lasombra Abyss that don't make it identical to other Dark Umbral phenomena. Locking down that one particular thing just doesn't ruin the whole mystery for me. I don't know enough about the crunch of V5 to know how much work might be necessary mechanically, but from a fluff standpoint I also don't see anything wrong with individual Storytellers deciding that the nature of the Abyss actually does differ from the 'canon' answer. Maybe the Abyss is a Zone, with close ties to Oblivion but plenty of other properties and metaphysical entanglements with other Realms?<br /> <br /> Also, not all &quot;darkness related stuff&quot; comes from the Abyss. There are two other Near Umbras plus the Deep Umbra that are all capable of producing darkness-related stuff. Maybe in Vampire everything is getting relegated to Oblivion/the Dark Umbra, but again, I don't see that as super concerning when we're talking about the Undead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except we have been told the only darkness related place now is the Abyss, those umbra places? Gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:23:36-07:00","id":1444684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444681#post1444681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except we have been told the only darkness related place now is the Abyss, those umbra places? Gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>And where was this mentioned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:26:01-07:00","id":1444686,"title":"","content":"It kinda is surprising because it's <i>wrong. </i> <br /> Oblivion is just destruction. You can't touch it. It just exists as an end. <br /> The Abyss is an expanse filled with malignant spirits. Only thing they got in common is that they're black and cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:37:57-07:00","id":1444692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444686#post1444686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda is surprising because it's <i>wrong. </i><br /> Oblivion is just destruction. You can't touch it. It just exists as an end.<br /> The Abyss is an expanse filled with malignant spirits. Only thing they got in common is that they're black and cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the bottom of the Labyrinth has been where demons (explictly they're the Neverborn, btw) have been since DEMON: THE FALLEN.<br /> <br /> Mind you, this is just WOD recycling.<br /> <br /> Why are the Demons of Demon: The Fallen in the Abyss/Labyrinth? Because they're replicating the mythology of Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:22:49-07:00","id":1444697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444684#post1444684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And where was this mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Twitter, Justin stated it, will look back when I have more time, but suck at twitter...so may not be able to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T14:29:12-07:00","id":1444715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444697#post1444697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Twitter, Justin stated it, will look back when I have more time, but suck at twitter...so may not be able to find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Justin posted &quot;lol Umbra ded&quot;?<br /> <br /> I have a hard time accepting that half of the World of Darkness cosmology can effectively and reasonably retconned by tweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T15:07:56-07:00","id":1444719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread#post1444431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thread for discussing all things Keeper.<br /> <br /> Oblivion vs. Obternation<br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla<br /> <br /> The remaining Lasombra back in the Sabbat<br /> <br /> Their new weakness<br /> <br /> How SHOULD the Lasombra have been updated<br /> <br /> Also, did Talley really kill Lucita or shall she be Regent?<br /> <br /> Here ya go!</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Oblivion vs. Obtenebration: </b>Not a fan. I preferred the hints, the ambiguity and the feeling that it might not be explainable or not shaped so the human mind could easily hold it. Maybe I'll backport Oblivion at some point for a path or two for Abyss Mystics. Also, this really needed some side plot making the Giovanni a Lasombra cuckoo in the Cappadocian nest, and their history is complicated enough as-is.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra joining the Camarilla:</b> <i>&quot;The Sabbat project has proven itself unworthy of our further support&quot; </i><br /> <br /> I always figured the Sabbat was not scared enough of Kine, had too many showelheads who believed the party line and did not spend enough resources on the Masquerade to keep up with kine recording tech. The Lasombra jumping ship as <i>Les Amis Noir</i> decided the Sabbat had outlived its usefulness was always in the cards.<br /> <br /> As far as I am concerned though, the Lasombra never managed to rid themselves entirely of the aura that they were doing the Camarilla a huge honor, and never quite got how no-one wanted them. Their <i>Antitribu</i> in particular. The Kings and Queens of Shadow turned out to be Lasombra in the end, and betrayed them at the convention of Prague, going over to the <i>Anttribu</i> <i>en masse</i> with their entire portfolio of resources and holdings. Leaving the main clan in a bit of a situation. It was one of the dangling plots I felt V5 just paved over.<br /> <br /> <b>Remaining Lasombra in the Sabbat:</b> Who?<br /> <br /> <b>New weakness: </b>I am a fan. I'll backport it. Its mainly for flavor though, only the elders will start to be seriously inconvenienced and methuselahs will be crippled. And they are not heavy tech users anyway. Unless I do an elders game it won't affect players. If I do, it'll be a curse of their abiltiy to do what they love slipping through their hands like sand. It'll generate in-world noddist speculation on how in ancient nights the curse was almost not noticeable and now it has grown to be crippling.<br /> <br /> <b>How SHOULD the Lasombra have been updated? </b>Kings and Queens of Shadow joining the antitribu. Arms of the Abyss reflavored to manipulating their own and other peoples shadows rather than &quot;tentacles&quot;. Black Metamorphosis replaced with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T21:30:03-07:00","id":1444772,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra is one of those clans that I think are strong in concept, but was improperly depicted in canon. And the V5 metaplot has really screwed things up for them.<br /> <br /> The major problem with both clanbooks is that they (as well as the Tzimisce clanbooks) forgot they were clans of the Sabbat. They ignored how the Sabbat has been depicted as creating new vampires. And they failed to distinguish what elements the main Lasombra clan and the anti-tribu should have in common and how they're different.<br /> <br /> I think there should be essentially three versions of the clan. All recognizably Lasombra, but easily differentiated from each other. <br /> <br /> The first are the Lasombra anti-tribu who should be a direct descendant of the Lasombra clan in the Dark Ages in the same way the Camarilla clans are, with adjustments as a result of seemingly losing their founder and working within the structure of the Camarilla. Relic clan institutions like the Friends of the Night still exist, but are forced to operate in secret as it violates the Sixth Tradition. They would carefully choose their childer like their Camarilla counterparts. They would support the more conservative and oppressive factions within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The second are the Sabbat Lasombra who represent the original Anarch Revolt. These were Lasombra who detested the oppression of the Lasombra elders of the Dark Ages and who fought for substantial changes in the clan culture. They would obviously hate an institution like the Friends of the Night, and they believe they have purged it in the \u201cnew\u201d Lasombra clan. They would follow the practice of random embraces as described in the original Sabbat descriptions. They may not necessarily be Loyalists, but should be fervent supporters of the ideals of the Anarch Revolt, although perhaps acting in a \u201cvanguard of the revolution\u201d kind of way. More practical about using power than the idealists of the Brujah anti-tribu for example.<br /> <br /> The third are those Lasombra of the Sabbat who joined the sect, but who fought against the Anarchs during the Anarch Revolt. Their membership in the sect is mostly based on cynical opportunism. They saw the bulk of their clan create the Sabbat. They did not see an opportunity for their clan to gain power through the Camarilla. So they joined the Sabbat in the century or two after the Convention of Thorns. They are very two faced, wanting to preserve elder power and old clan traditions in a sect that should be hostile to them. They have to balance things \u2013 appearing to create their children through the random creation rates, but actually selecting them as much as they can. They still practice the courts of the Friends of the Night in secret, culling other Lasombra in an attempt to rebuild the clan. But they still revile the anti-tribu as traitors for joining their enemies. They are the cancer and hypocrisy within the Sabbat, but their leadership has been critical for the sect's survival. In culture, they are a blend of the anti-tribu and other Sabbat Lasombra. They are equally fervent in their support of the Sabbat, but this is demonstrated in different ways than the mass of the Sabbat Lasombra. They don't support &quot;freedom&quot; in other way, but they are often at the head of other things that distinguish the Sabbat, like development of the Paths of Enlightenment, supporting Crusades, etc. This creates a lot of tension within the Sabbat Lasombra.<br /> <br /> As for Disciplines, I can't comment on Oblivion, but felt certain levels of Obtenebration were too powerful. It should never have been a combat Discipline. Since the Lasombra already have two active, forceful Disciplines in Dominate and Potence, Obtenebration should have been a less forceful Discipline. I don't like its more cartoonish powers that resemble Marvel Comic's Darkforce rather than traditional vampire powers. Control over shadows and darkness should not mean the darkness can punch you.<br /> <br /> Since I haven't read V5 I can only comment given my perception based on how people have reacted on these forums. But it seems the defection of Lasombra into the Camarilla wasn't properly predicated. I have not heard once how these defectors could have overcome the vaulderie and vinculum to do so, or why the Camarilla would have trusted such defectors if they were still in effect. This is just lazy writing.<br /> <br /> If one wanted a situation where the Sabbat imploded, a Civil War broke out, and mass defection occurred, there is an \u201ceasy\u201d way to justify that. And that is for the vaulderie to stop working and vinculum to no longer exist. This would happen suddenly and mysteriously. But it could work as metaplot and justify a lot of what happened. I personally would not have liked such a change in the setting. But at least it would explain why things happened.<br /> <br /> I liked the original weakness of the Lasombra. It was a standard flaw of vampires so it needed to show up somewhere. I understand the concern of people that in today's age that the weakness might up being a benefit as Lasombra would seem immune to video surveillance. However, there needed to be more thinking behind it. The purpose of the weakness was to make the Lasombra more vulnerable as detection as vampires. So any changes should have built on that. At the top of my head, the easiest change would have been to show some kind of distortion on video equipment rather than simply being invisible so that there could be a trigger for people to know something went wrong. That has flaws too, but at least it doesn't change things too much and seems more like a clarification rather than a change.<br /> <br /> If one really wanted the Lasombra anti-tribu to become more prominent in the Camarilla, it should have had more natural origins than a ham fisted metaplot worthy of professional wrestling. Show how the anti-tribu have benefitted the sept, accrued boons, built influence from a position of weakness, and perhaps even grow normally like cementing the Camarilla's position in Latin America. Then at the right time they made a pitch to finally be recognized in the Inner Circle and they were. And now they're a more prominent part of the Camarilla, whether you go with the original 7 clans (the only right choice IMO) or the ridiculous V5 version that now exists.<br /> <br /> I don't care anything at all for the signature characters of an RPG. So Lucita is utterly irrelevant. In so far she exists, I'd prefer it to be as a background character representing something a PC could be. In this case, it'd be a PC elder, but that's fine. Elders as PCs go back to the Elysium supplement. Like many such sect defections, her defection to the Sabbat in the Revised era was not well supported. As a long time anti-tribu enemy, the Sabbat Lasombra should just want her dead. It's like the British welcoming back Kim Philby with full miltary honors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T21:40:07-07:00","id":1444774,"title":"","content":"The difference between the Lasombra of the Anarch Revolt and the Antitribu has always been rather huge, though. One of the things that should be remembered is the fact that the Anarch Revolt amongst the Lasombra was one carried out at the top down, not one that was carried from the bottom up. The leader of the Lasombra Anarchs was Gratiano, a.k.a. a frigging 4th Generation Vampire. He may have been the Prince Harry of the family but he was still a Prince. Not a Baron, Count, or Duke let alone a peasant. Gratiano walked into the castle of the Lasombra Antediluvian because he was a guy who belonged there.<br /> <br /> The reason the Lasombra &quot;won&quot; their Anarch Revolt is because the moment that the Antediluvian was dead, everyone did switch their allegiance. The idea being that &quot;cynical opportunism&quot; is actually something that is ADMIRED among the Lasombra. Montano, a vampire who was older than dirt and of somewhat noble character (as ancient fiends go), was the one who was the odd man out for wanting to continue the fight and not siding with the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> If not for the Friends of the Night, he should be head of the Clan because he's older than dirt himself. Instead, they sided with Gratiano because the Clan's leadership chose to endorse the act of patricide and diablerie that Gratiano supposedly committed. I have my suspicions they may have been ordered to do so by Lasombra himself because it's not like they would ever know their own thoughts were not their own. We also do know that Lasombra arranged for the faking of his death and has literally been hanging around in his own castle this entire time when not possessing Gratiano. Why? Who knows. Antediluvians can get bored too some days I guess.<br /> <br /> From a Watsonian point of view, this helps set up the events of V5 because it is established that the Lasombra are a clan with no honor. When their Antediluvian fell, they immediately turned traitor on his former loyalists. When the Sabbat discovered Lasombra was still alive and were going on a very dangerous self-destructive crusade, they switched sides again. Why? Because they are a bunch of scheming seflish bastards among a race of scheming selfish bastards.<br /> <br /> Now, the writers didn't HAVE to write the Lasombra this way but they have ALWAYS written the Lasombra this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I haven't read V5 I can only comment given my perception based on how people have reacted on these forums. But it seems the defection of Lasombra into the Camarilla wasn't properly predicated. I have not heard once how these defectors could have overcome the vaulderie and vinculum to do so, or why the Camarilla would have trusted such defectors if they were still in effect. This is just lazy writing. </div> </div> </div>The Vinculum has never made you loyal to the Sabbat. The Vinculum makes you loyal to your pack mates. Nothing would stop you from defecting even if you might hesitate to kill them. Oddly, it might mean that if a Lasombra defects then he'll possibly bring his posse with him. Given the nature of the Gehenna War, I'm pretty sure that plenty of Lasombra did lose long term packmates or the defectors were primarily Lasombra loyal to other Lasombra alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T21:42:13-07:00","id":1444775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444772#post1444772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one really wanted the Lasombra anti-tribu to become more prominent in the Camarilla, it should have had more natural origins than a ham fisted metaplot worthy of professional wrestling. Show how the anti-tribu have benefitted the sept, accrued boons, built influence from a position of weakness, and perhaps even grow normally like cementing the Camarilla's position in Latin America. Then at the right time they made a pitch to finally be recognized in the Inner Circle and they were. And now they're a more prominent part of the Camarilla, whether you go with the original 7 clans (the only right choice IMO) or the ridiculous V5 version that now exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I absolutely agree with. After the defection of the Brujah and the Gangrel, it would not be surprising for the Lasombra antitribu to suddenly wield a lot more power in a much diminished sect, paving the way for them to step up and become a major force within the Camarilla, essentially stepping into the shoes of one of the other two clans who left. That would have made a lot more sense for pushing the Labomsbra into being a major Camarilla player characters than what we ended up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T21:45:53-07:00","id":1444776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444775#post1444775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I absolutely agree with. After the defection of the Brujah and the Gangrel, it would not be surprising for the Lasombra antitribu to suddenly wield a lot more power in a much diminished sect, paving the way for them to step up and become a major force within the Camarilla, essentially stepping into the shoes of one of the other two clans who left. That would have made a lot more sense for pushing the Labomsbra into being a major Camarilla player characters than what we ended up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually what happened. It was the Antitribu who invited the Lasombra over to increase their own power. Notably, it was the most famous Lasombra of all, Marcus Vitel who arranged for the defection with the Amis Noctis.<br /> <br /> That's why Talley was helping it happen.<br /> <br /> This despite the fact that Marcus is presently an Anarch. But as I've always said, Methusalehs think of sects as a stupid fiction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T22:09:02-07:00","id":1444779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444715#post1444715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Justin posted &amp;quot;lol Umbra ded&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> I have a hard time accepting that half of the World of Darkness cosmology can effectively and reasonably retconned by tweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he tweeted that the cosmology of the game lines was going to be unified and we didn't need multiple realms for the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T22:27:58-07:00","id":1444780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444779#post1444779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, he tweeted that the cosmology of the game lines was going to be unified and we didn't need multiple realms for the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer the Fae to be part of the Middle Umbra than Dreaming.<br /> <br /> One Spirit World for one World of Darkness!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T22:41:50-07:00","id":1444781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444779#post1444779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, he tweeted that the cosmology of the game lines was going to be unified and we didn't need multiple realms for the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kind of vague, and I would probably want to see what actually comes out of that before stating, for example, that the Deep Umbra will no longer exist.<br /> <br /> I can agree that it's likely to mean some &quot;mysteries&quot; being cleared up, some things being retconned, others simplified. And I can understand and sympathize with people who would prefer more of that stuff to be left to &quot;mystery.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if what you're arguing is that they are going to try and set up cosmology in a way that will likely make crossover play more functional... I am probably on the top ten, maybe five, list of &quot;worst people to make that argument to.&quot; xD<br /> <br /> Again, we'll see what the results look like, though my understanding is that we're a long way from W/M5, where those kinds of issues can reasonably be expect to be explored. Even if they do clear some things up and simplify others, I would be surprised if they intend to take the mystery out of everything in favour of a purely &quot;D&amp;D-style&quot; adventure-romp cosmology. But at the moment, it's all just a hypothetical future. This conversation right here might have some influence on what that looks like.<br /> <br /> But anyone who wants anything other than Vampire is probably gonna be playing 20A or earlier editions for a while, so it's kind of moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T22:46:48-07:00","id":1444782,"title":"","content":"I don't think Tweets are canon either, though TV tropes would define it as &quot;Word of Saint Paul.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say authoritative but not approved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But anyone who wants anything other than Vampire is probably gonna be playing 20A or earlier editions for a while, so it's kind of moot. </div> </div> </div>Weird how there's Werewolf video games and Wraith ones but not updated games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T23:05:21-07:00","id":1444785,"title":"","content":"Eh, not really. Games are safe, you can fuck with tabletop mechanics completely and it'd be fine because &quot;videogame&quot;. Like if Call of Duty (esp CoD4 and onwards) represented an acceptable grasp of modern warfare then Bloodlines represents an acceptable grasp of the more natural tabletop world. Essentially, they can take liberties. Also a linear games means you only need to represent a small part of the universe and don't fuck up the cannon on a grand scale.<br /> <br /> V5 just puts W5 in a wierd spot because, well, V5 turned an allegorically political game into an overt political one, and a lot of people really didn't like that, what are they going to do with a game that started out offensive and overtly political, one in which being a tribal is part of the core experience? Especially since a lot of strong opinions bled into V5 and you wouldn't want a zealous... Fianna to define the Uktena would you? Also V5's combat mechanics are designed to gloss over combat and Werewolf is literally about being a murder-machine wolf-warrior fighting for the planet... could you imagine a version of Mortal Combat or UFC designed to gloss over combat? But then again I suppose I feel like the Lasombra in V5 were written by someone who hates the Lasombra. I'm sure they'll tell me they love the Lasombra, just like how you tell us you love the Tzmisce and the Sabbat, when really you mean Dracula and... probably the loyalist faction or something that doesn't represent the Sabbat in the view of the majority.<br /> <br /> How horribly off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T23:16:19-07:00","id":1444786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444785#post1444785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, not really. Games are safe, you can fuck with tabletop mechanics completely and it'd be fine because &quot;videogame&quot;. Like if Call of Duty (esp CoD4 and onwards) represented an acceptable grasp of modern warfare then Bloodlines represents an acceptable grasp of the more natural tabletop world. Essentially, they can take liberties. Also a linear games means you only need to represent a small part of the universe and don't fuck up the cannon on a grand scale.<br /> <br /> V5 just puts W5 in a wierd spot because, well, V5 turned an allegorically political game into an overt political one, and a lot of people really didn't like that, what are they going to do with a game that started out offensive and overtly political, one in which being a tribal is part of the core experience? Especially since a lot of strong opinions bled into V5 and you wouldn't want a zealous... Fianna to define the Uktena would you? .</div> </div> </div> </div>HEART OF THE FOREST is actually a really good game for updating Werewolf to 5th Edition. It strongly accented the environmental element while also toning down the violence. The funny thing about EARTHBLOOD is it actually dials up the violence as you slaughter hundreds of regular human beings in that game that would normally flee from the Garou due to the Delerium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also V5's combat mechanics are designed to gloss over combat and Werewolf is literally about being a murder-machine wolf-warrior fighting for the planet... could you imagine a version of Mortal Combat or UFC designed to gloss over combat? But then again I suppose I feel like the Lasombra in V5 were written by someone who hates the Lasombra. I'm sure they'll tell me they love the Lasombra, just like how you tell us you love the Tzmisce and the Sabbat, when really you mean Dracula and... probably the loyalist faction or something that doesn't represent the Sabbat in the view of the majority.<br /> <br /> How horribly off topic </div> </div> </div>Well it was written by Matthew Dawkins so you can take it up with him. He was the one who made the pitch for the Lasombra to join the Camarilla after the Followers of Set didn't. Also, to clarify, Dracula is who I think the Tzimisce should resemble but I love all of the Dark Age Tzimisce. Lord Ruthven, The Vukudlak, the Voivodes as a whole, Vladimir Rustovich, Vykos, the Dracon, and Shaagra. They had panache back then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think the Tzimisce shouldn't be <i>Necroscope </i>vampires as they don't fit V:TM.<br /> <br /> And I love the Sabbat. They're my second favorite sect. Their absence from V5 is their biggest flaw. A V:TM without the Sabbat is far lesser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T23:23:34-07:00","id":1444788,"title":"","content":"I mean, my reaction to &quot;Weird how there are games but not new editions&quot; was basically: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/016/729/large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> If you want to talk about Tzimisce, maybe I'll bump the thread (if there is one) with my feelings on what I found out about V5 Tzimisce recently. But yeah, off topic.<br /> <br /> And I'm generally on the side of saying that a lot of what I know about V5, as an outsider, seems rather ham-fisted, so I'm not especially surprised that it was maybe not fleshed out as well as it should have been. But the concept itself doesn't strike me as off, for reasons noted above, so it doesn't really surprise or bother me. Just another thing V5 did in a clumsy fashion.<br /> <br /> Also, was not aware that Talley killed(?) Lucita. CbN V5 thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T23:33:24-07:00","id":1444789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444788#post1444788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Also, was not aware that Talley killed(?) Lucita. CbN V5 thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's suggested it's happen but not canon.<br /> <br /> And yes, please do bump it or make a new thread.<br /> <br /> V5 Companion thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion/page33\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mpanion/page33</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T04:08:07-07:00","id":1444810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444788#post1444788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to talk about Tzimisce, maybe I'll bump the thread (if there is one) with my feelings on what I found out about V5 Tzimisce recently. But yeah, off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stickied <i>V5 vs V20</i> thread or the <i>V5 Companion</i> thread might be a good place to discuss Tzimisce changes. I'd be interested to know what you think, as I have pretty strong feeling about their overhaul, myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion\"> V5 Vampire Companion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1428599-v5-vampire-companion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Today will see the publication of the V5 Vampire Companion. It will be home to rules for V5 Ravnos, Tzimisce, Salubri, ghouls and will also be home to unimaginable </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-vs-v20-thread</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","user":"Garygeneric","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T04:10:29-07:00","id":1444811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444780#post1444780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd prefer the Fae to be part of the Middle Umbra than Dreaming.<br /> <br /> One Spirit World for one World of Darkness!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely know the few fans C:TD has would absolutely hate this and this is a laughable idea on its own. The Dreaming was its quasi-&quot;own thing&quot; (scratch that, it mostly WAS its own thing), but it also basically was tacked/keyed to be of the High Umbra. This is because that part of the Umbra is the most influenced by the ideas and concepts of things, especially from the mortals. The Middle-Umbra however exists and has its own ebbs independent from ideals formed by the unconscious.<br /> <br /> There is simply absolutely no reason for the Dreaming to be apart of the Middle Umbra. And if they should go with the lazy move of consolidating the Dreaming and not have its own thing anymore, it'd be better off just being apart of the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> Honestly for any more Umbra development, they should get the actual writers who from the past who actually wrote them or have the most experience with it as to not damage the franchise more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:04:28-07:00","id":1444826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444811#post1444811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely know the few fans C:TD has would absolutely hate this and this is a laughable idea on its own. The Dreaming was its quasi-&amp;quot;own thing&amp;quot; (scratch that, it mostly WAS its own thing), but it also basically was tacked/keyed to be of the High Umbra. This is because that part of the Umbra is the most influenced by the ideas and concepts of things, especially from the mortals. The Middle-Umbra however exists and has its own ebbs independent from ideals formed by the unconscious.<br /> <br /> There is simply absolutely no reason for the Dreaming to be apart of the Middle Umbra. And if they should go with the lazy move of consolidating the Dreaming and not have its own thing anymore, it'd be better off just being apart of the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> Honestly for any more Umbra development, they should get the actual writers who from the past who actually wrote them or have the most experience with it as to not damage the franchise more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded on Far being far more associated with the High Umbra (to the extent the Dreaming maps to anything), but my fear given their past \u2018streamlining\u2019 (see Clan Hecata) and tendencies towards pulling bits from NWoD/CoD is that \u2018unification\u2019 will be a rehash of the Supernal Realms where there are exactly five otherworlds (basically angels, demons, fae, nature spirits and the dead), no more no less.<br /> <br /> And honestly, we saw a move towards this even in Revised; where the Malfeans of Werewolf and Nephandi were declared to just be the twosted dreams of the Neverborn Malfeans in the Labyrinth and then the biblical demons went from being high umbral reflections of human belief to entities trapped under the underworld.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s already two things that were tied to the middle/deep and high Umbra redefined to be instead part of the low/dark Umbra. Throw in redefining the Obtenabration as Oblivion connected to the same place as the demons are locked up and you get a rather reductionist cosmology where as much as possible is being smooshed into the same space.<br /> <br /> As such it wouldn\u2019t surprise me to see the spirit worlds of the fae and changing breeds smooshed together into a \u201cthrough the looking glass\u201d reflection of the world which sits just above the Underworld of Wraith and maybe a celestial realm above... basically an Olympus/Heaven &gt; Spirit World &gt; Hades/Underworld &gt; Tartarus/Abyss arrangement with the bare minimum needed for the various splats to function, while unintentionally nuking something really important they overlooked (ex. How are the Ethernauts supposed to plumb the depths of such a reductionist cosmos?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:14:45-07:00","id":1444828,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned nothing in the Vaulderie prevents you from defecting from the sabbat. I would disagree. Funny enough this is in Lasombra Clanbook Revised page 56.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Successfully leaving the Sabbat takes time. A vampire with extensive Vinculum bonds probably can\u2019t do it at all. The knowledge that she is joining the enemy and fighting against her former allies is sufficient to make unlife uncomfortable with a Vinculum bond of 3 or higher, difficult at 6 or higher and almost altogether impossible above 7. The would-be defector must remove her allies herself or wait for time and chance to do it for her. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:31:59-07:00","id":1444830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">tendencies towards pulling bits from <b>NWoD/CoD</b> is that \u2018unification\u2019 will be a <b>rehash</b> of the Supernal Realms</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this pattern aswell too and this practically has been the case with V5 so far; though even players who are native only to nWoD/VtR even say that the things nu-Wolf take/attempt to adapt, is done in such a horrible way that supposedly makes the original source of inspiration &quot;look bad&quot;. One can even imagine how badly the oWoD Umbra will be borked if they try to adapt nWoD's understanding of cosmology into it, but much somehow much more worse.<br /> <br /> Even then, just simply doing the streamline/dumb-down method won't work in this case with how they've been doing oWoD so far in this case. Too many new questions and gaping lorebreaks would appear from conveniently &quot;merging&quot; all the Umbrae or specific things or places. Look how they borked up Obtenebration and Necromancy in one fell swoop for the laziness of congregating it just for the so-called &quot;Oblivion&quot; Discipline.<br /> <br /> Even like on what we agreed on earlier about if in ANY possible scenario of the Dreaming being dumb-downed; and it being subsequently folded into the High Umbra; still on its own wouldn't make any sense. The Dreaming by itself has its own lore weaved into it that doesn't broach much as what went on, or goes on in the High Umbra. The only tenuous similarity they bare is both being heavily shaped by the schema of thought itself; but the difference in them lies in the fact that the High Umbra is more toward the cerebral line of thinking and knowing; while the Dreaming is much more of the happy ups and nightmarish downs of unconscious or imaginative lane-line of thought. This is why the Dreaming when developed most likely was drafted into its own thing.<br /> <br /> I honestly think V5 shouldn't be touching or doing new stuff with the Umbra at all by this point. In pre-V5 for VTM, that aspect was never really dwelt with to begin with; And when its time to get around to revisiting the Umbra when W5 and the subsequent rest start coming along, they should get the original writers of most of the Umbrae or anyone among White Wolf with the most experience with that part of oWoD to begin redeveloping it for new editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:28:05-07:00","id":1444835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444811#post1444811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I definitely know the few fans C:TD has would absolutely hate this and this is a laughable idea on its own. more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling: The Dreaming was my first game, one that I played on the old White Wolf forums, and I'm mentioned in the thanks of the final book published for the original line. Why do you think CHANGE is always going to be hated by fans?<br /> <br /> It's pretty insulting to fans to believe we're all so closed minded and boring that we're only interested in rehashing old material and not improving it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444828#post1444828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was mentioned nothing in the Vaulderie prevents you from defecting from the sabbat. I would disagree. Funny enough this is in Lasombra Clanbook Revised page 56.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, that seems to go against the rules as established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:43:53-07:00","id":1444840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think CHANGE is always going to be hated by fans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why in the world do you think merging into the Dreaming into the Middle Umbra would be a good idea at all? Have you read Werewolf? And how long have you parsed over Dreaming? These realms have mostly nothing alike whatsoever. Chimerical reality is totally different from the Spirit Wilds reality in how they operate. Attempting to merge the Dreaming and Middle Umbra would also be a huge nonsensical asspull to begin with. I even highly doubt (but not hopeful whatsoever) that nu-Wolf would even do anything like this idea at all.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And what you suggest for C:TD isn't even improvement, its just destruction. There is no reason from any lore or atmosphere point to converge the Dreaming and the Middle Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:47:38-07:00","id":1444842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444840#post1444840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why in the world do you think merging into the Dreaming into the Middle Umbra would be a good idea at all? Have you read Werewolf? And how long have you parsed over Dreaming? These realms have mostly nothing alike whatsoever. Chimerical reality is totally different from the Spirit Wilds reality in how they operate. Attempting to merge the Dreaming and Middle Umbra would also be a huge nonsensical asspull to begin with. I even highly doubt (but not hopeful whatsoever) that nu-Wolf would even do anything like this idea at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there should be one Spirit World and an infinite one. The Dreaming should just be part of the larger one. Frankly, I think it makes more sense for each line to have confusion about the nature of the various spirits than say there's multiple groups of roughly similar things that are completely different.<br /> <br /> Since every Spirit World is infinite, it's not even like it would be noticed if the Dreaming was a Middle Umbra Realm.<br /> <br /> It would, however, allow more crossover in both settings and more setting verisimilitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:58:43-07:00","id":1444843,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, no. There is no real reason for the Dreaming to be apart of the Middle Umbra. The basic fiat of how Chimerical reality is intrinsically different from how the Middle Umbra is that it is more somewhat more grounded, but of course esoteric in its own ways; but not in the sense of how the Dreaming is easily shaped by the suggestion of dreams or imagination. This also doesn't even even to go on how if anything as previously mentioned, the Dreaming would be fit more-so for the High Umbra; but this wouldn't be ideal either. It really should just be its own thing like it already has.<br /> <br /> Stop clamoring for things for things to be destroyed or be &quot;retrofitted&quot; where it doesn't need it. Instead more better suggestions would be to expand upon the Dreaming from what was left off after the close of C:TD. See how the Dreaming has shaped and changed since past 1999; but as its OWN thing, not subsumed into the lane of the Middle Umbra/Werewolf. And the whole one &quot;Spirit World&quot; nonsense and the idea of clabbering all the Umbra into one thing is another ludicrous idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:05:03-07:00","id":1444846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444843#post1444843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, no. There is no real reason for the Dreaming to be apart of the Middle Umbra. The basic fiat of how Chimerical reality is intrinsically different from how the Middle Umbra is more somewhat more grounded, but of course esoteric in its own ways; but not in the sense of how the Dreaming is easily shaped by the suggestion of dreams or imagination. This also doesn't even even to go on how if anything as previously mentioned, the Dreaming would be fit more-so for the High Umbra; but this wouldn't be ideal either. It really should just be its own thing like it already has.<br /> <br /> Stop clamoring for things for things to be destroyed or be &quot;retrofitted&quot; where it doesn't need it. Instead more better suggestions would be to expand upon the Dreaming from what was left off after the close of C:TD. See how the Dreaming has shaped and changed since past 1999; but as its OWN thing, not subsumed into the lane of the Middle Umbra/Werewolf. And the whole one &quot;Spirit World&quot; nonsense and the idea of clabbering all the Umbra into one thing is another ludicrous idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give a reason why, from a non-in universe perspective, why it is worse for the line and not better for it? A lot of the objections I see seem to boil down to, &quot;It was always like that and changing it is bad.&quot; I don't see a reason why it is more fun and engaging for Storytellers as well as players. which should be the primary reason for any changes, IMHO.<br /> <br /> This applies to the Lasombra as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:08:58-07:00","id":1444847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444835#post1444835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think CHANGE is always going to be hated by fans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disney remakes, Disney Star Wars (sans Mandalorian), Star Trek 2009, Doctor Who, She-Ra reboot, DC Comic's Nu52, D&amp;D 4E, NWoD, V5, this link (<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheyChangedItNowItSucks\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...edItNowItSucks</a>)...<br /> <br /> Seriously... what planet are you living on where fans haven't despised even minor changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:12:26-07:00","id":1444849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444847#post1444847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disney remakes, Disney Star Wars (sans Mandalorian), Star Trek 2009, Doctor Who, She-Ra reboot, DC Comic's Nu52, D&amp;D 4E, NWoD, V5, this link (<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheyChangedItNowItSucks\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...edItNowItSucks</a>)...<br /> <br /> Seriously... what planet are you living on where fans haven't despised even minor changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you got me there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:17:41-07:00","id":1444852,"title":"","content":"Because it subordinates C:TD out of its own auspice, game narrative, and agency. That should be obvious on its own. The Dreaming in mechanic and theme is entirely different in theme from how the Middle Umbra pans out thematically in its own mechanic and theme.<br /> <br /> Like I mentioned before; the Dreaming has moments/moods of either either happy-go-luckiness of imaginative randomness, or it has times of sudden nightmarish freakish lulls that is full of horror. There is no real inbetween, or if so, very rare. Its shaped, molded, and ebbs in a pattern of Dreams among other things. This is different from the Middle Umbra entirely, which is influenced by environment itself on the other side of the Gauntlet than rather being shaped by aforementioned Dreams. <br /> <br /> The Middle Umbra/Spirit Worlds is almost always serious and foreboding. Its full of suspense, but awe aswell due to the sheer spirituality of it. It also has facets of the Wyrm, Weaver, and the Wyld that are more centric and relevant only to W:TA. You could maybe try and draw lines to the Wyld concurrently with the generalness of the Dreaming, but that still wouldn't work since the Wyld is a Thing Unto Itself, and isn't on the suggestive whims of collective thought or creativity; its the thing with its entire purpose and sphere IS breaking reality on its own. And its chaos aswell is its own too. <br /> <br /> I seriously just don't understand why in the world like I ask before, on why you think its a good idea to merge the Dreaming into the Middle Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:30:03-07:00","id":1444855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444852#post1444852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously just don't understand why in the world like I ask before, on why you think its a good idea to merge the Dreaming into the Middle Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I told you, to make crossover easier and to also enrich the lore by making it clear that each supernatural group has ties as well as different ways of looking at the same concept. Like the old Buddhist proverb of a dozen blind monks feeling an elephant to describe religion.<br /> <br /> One of the earliest Werewolf supplements, THE BOOK OF THE WYRM 1st Edition, described a caern that existed as an enormous flying buttress cathedral surrounded by a bunch of decapitated flying heads created by a serial killer's actions in an apartment complex. Basically, some serious SILENT HILL 4: THE ROOM bullshit. It wasn't that the serial killer was magical, he wasn't. It was just the intensity of the serial killer's visions and evil actions created the enormous cathedral in the Penumbra and a Black Spiral Dancer later consecrated it.<br /> <br /> As such, I've always felt that the link between human belief structures and the Middle Umbra should be stronger, especially since Mage flat out confirms that the High Umbra is full of countless gods, demons, angels, and so on that have been shaped by human beliefs. Part of why Demon: The Fallen is kind of the odd pony out is due to the fact that there's already five or six YHVHS in the High Umbra with the Black Furies the only ones who think its the Patriarch versus, say, a manifestation of Jupiter or Helios.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Dreaming is something that isn't taken quite as seriously as the rest of the Spirit Worlds in Mage, Werewolf, and so on when there's no reason that they shouldn't be. The difference between a Manifested Nexus Crawler and a tentacled shoggoth horror chimera using Wyrd is fundamentally the same since they end up horrifically murdering humans. Things like Bygones also were clearly MEANT to be Changelings or chimera but they chickened the hell out and made them different despite it making no goddamn sense.<br /> <br /> Maybe I erroneously believe that the Changeling: The Dreaming lineage deserves better than its gotten (answer: yes, yes it does) but part of the reason its not taken seriously is that its creatures like chimera and the fae themselves aren't taken as seriously as Formor, Banes, Bygones, and other things that fill its ecological niche in the setting. I say cut out the middle man and make it clear that the Changelings ARE spirit possessed humans with their own rules. The same way Lupines are werewolves, so are humans rotted out by Thallain spirits how other races perceive possessing changelings.<br /> <br /> Changelings vs. Formori<br /> Changelings vs. Nephandi<br /> Changelings vs. Fallen<br /> <br /> There's already Demon and Angel Kith in C20.<br /> <br /> More streamlined, more interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:56:03-07:00","id":1444866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Dreaming is something that isn't taken quite as seriously as the rest of the Spirit Worlds in Mage, Werewolf, and so on when there's no reason that they shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes; the genius take from this summation is to relegate the Dreaming not as its own thing and just cobbler it with the Low Umbra. That would definitely would make it be taken &quot;seriously&quot;. You literally think deconstructing the thing that makes Changeling onto its own and makes it unique will somehow help or get it &quot;taken seriously&quot;...? The very thing where most of Changeling's background comes from and where literally the sum of all its development eked cursively with? That's very funny. Its even more laughable that you say Changeling &quot;deserves better than its gotten&quot;, while in the SAME literal breadth clamor an idea that the Dreaming of all things should be nonsensically subsumed into the Middle Umbra. <br /> <br /> If YOU don't think Changeling is serious on its own, that's your thing. But to suggest that Dreaming needs to be torn into another aspect of the Umbra it barely has any thematic, atmospheric, or narrative connection with; is suggesting you don't even understand the game itself. It's literally in the title itself, Changeling: &quot;THE DREAMING&quot;; not Changeling: &quot;THE SPIRIT WILDS&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:57:33-07:00","id":1444867,"title":"","content":"I don't think you got my argument. The idea that you think I don't take Changeling seriously when I want it to be part of the backgrounds of all the major gamelines versus being segregated off is silly to me. Then again, I really want a streamlined and linked World of Darkness with shared rules as well as creatures as well as mythology.<br /> <br /> I get the impression you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:05:07-07:00","id":1444868,"title":"","content":"Off Topic, folks!<br /> <br /> If you want to make or bump a thread elsewhere, maybe I'll chime in with some fence-sitting. But we are very far away from the Lasombra now, beyond the vaguest conceptual links. Bring your speculations about how X5 will save/ruin the Cosmology of the WoD back to the Vampires at least <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: looks like the last &quot;on topic&quot; comment had to do with the Vaulderie being described in ways that *would* mess up the Lasombra Defection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:13:49-07:00","id":1444870,"title":"","content":"I directly addressed it, but sure. If you mean not going into your blurb about the Middle Umbra along with the High Umbra in your previous post, it's dodgy aswell. The High Umbra also operates almost entirely different from the Middle Umbra. Even in posts above, I already address the points you claim I don't understand.<br /> <br /> The Middle Umbra isn't shaped by human belief structures for the most part, the Middle Umbra is mostly sovereign onto itself. The local environment mostly has an influence on the Middle Umbra, which is one of the central themes of Werewolf to begin with.<br /> <br /> The High Umbra on the other hand is rightly inferenced to be more malleable to the &quot;thought-stream&quot; of things from mortals, and that's correct, that is how it works. This is why this particular Umbra has always been aligned with Mage, which heavily has the theme of its Consensus motif going on.<br /> <br /> However where you go off the rails;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, I've always felt that the link <b>between human belief structures and the Middle Umbra should be stronger, especially since Mage</b> flat out confirms that the High Umbra is full of countless gods, demons, angels, and so on that have been shaped by human beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think just because one Umbra does something, it has to be the same in another one? You do know why they're narratively and thematically different Umbrae to begin with, right? So your argument by doesn't make sense and is dodgy like I said. And this roundabouts to the other points I touched on about; the Dreaming aswell also has a different theme, approach, and narrative.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to merge with the Middle Umbra, and doing such to fit your view &quot;that it needs to be 'cuz the High Umbra does stuff with mortal-'umie thoughts, so errrrrr, put the Dreaming in the Middle Umbra so the latt'ah can do the same&quot; makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: looks like the last &quot;on topic&quot; comment had to do with the Vaulderie being described in ways that *would* mess up the Lasombra Defection</div> </div> </div> </div>Its simple. The narrative of the game was broken just for the simple fact that nu-Wolf wanted a way to hamfist the Lasombra into the Camarilla; even despite established facets in the lore and even the game mechanics (read: Vaulderie).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:14:13-07:00","id":1444871,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to make the Middle Umbra and the Dreaming the same. Werewolf already has a concept where the Garou and Changelings interact - it's the Near Realm of Arcadia Gateway. It was explicitly part of the Dreaming in second edition. It wasn't until Revised that suddenly the inhabitants there weren't fae, but some kind of spirit emanation. That didn't prevent Changeling, in its Dreams &amp; Nightmares sourcebook which described the Dreaming geography, to describe the &quot;Far Dreaming&quot; - which was obviously the same thing as the Arcadia Gateway. The details of various &quot;realms of interest&quot; are identical to the description of areas in the Arcadia Gateway.<br /> <br /> Plus the Umbral domains of Trods are the Green Paths of Balor in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> No one needs to reinvent the wheel if you want more Garou &amp; Changeling crossover. The Garou have always had the ability to enter the Dreaming if they wanted, and therefore logically fae and changelings can cross over into the Middle Umbra. It's just that the developers of the Revised era wanted to downplay it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:21:31-07:00","id":1444872,"title":"","content":"Yeah, yeah, I'll drop it. Anyone wants to discuss cosmology in another thread then I'll do it. But this is the Lasombra thread as stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:42:28-07:00","id":1444877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444872#post1444872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, yeah, I'll drop it. Anyone wants to discuss cosmology in another thread then I'll do it. But this is the Lasombra thread as stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'll throw something into the General Forum after work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But on the topic of the Vinculum inhibiting the Lasombra defection, I've previously mentioned that I imagine a lot of &quot;low level&quot; Lasombra pack members as being likely to stick around, because they seem the most likely to have built up a large number of Vinculum ties to Cainites outside their own Clan. But given that Clan structures have seemed to largely remain intact in the Sabbat, rather than being overtaken by a melting-pot Sect monoculture entirely, I can imagine that a lot of older Lasombra probably have Vinculum bonds mostly, if not entirely, with other Lasombra. Those bonds wouldn't get in the way if all the Lasombra you have a Vinculum with are coming along for a ride. And that's not to mention the frequency with which powerful or Elderly Sabbat &quot;members&quot; often get away with being exceptions to things like the Vaulderie, because the Sect has frequently made compromises of that sort to stay strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:56:33-07:00","id":1444883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444877#post1444877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'll throw something into the General Forum after work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But on the topic of the Vinculum inhibiting the Lasombra defection, I've previously mentioned that I imagine a lot of &quot;low level&quot; Lasombra pack members as being likely to stick around, because they seem the most likely to have built up a large number of Vinculum ties to Cainites outside their own Clan. But given that Clan structures have seemed to largely remain intact in the Sabbat, rather than being overtaken by a melting-pot Sect monoculture entirely, I can imagine that a lot of older Lasombra probably have Vinculum bonds mostly, if not entirely, with other Lasombra. Those bonds wouldn't get in the way if all the Lasombra you have a Vinculum with are coming along for a ride. And that's not to mention the frequency with which powerful or Elderly Sabbat &quot;members&quot; often get away with being exceptions to things like the Vaulderie, because the Sect has frequently made compromises of that sort to stay strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, my own thoughts are more, &quot;If anyone knows how to game the system and break the Vinculum bonds then it will be the Amis Noctis.&quot; I honestly think they could probably snap it with an Abyssal ritual of some kind and never think twice about it.<br /> <br /> Plus, we know the Sabbat has countless civil wars and duels to the death. Defecting shouldn't be that harder if you think it's for the good of the Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:01:13-07:00","id":1444886,"title":"","content":"How many centuries has the Sabbat run for up to this point, and with along that, the Vinculum one of the main components on why it remained together? The whole point of it in the first place was to prohibit the car crash scenario that is the Lasombra &quot;mass defection&quot;. And the Sabbat within itself wouldn't be stupid to allow the majority of the Lasombra to have Vaulderie only done among their own clan only, barring inferences toward a theory that since &quot;no monoculture of the Sabbat (the Sabbat certainly DOES have a culture, all the Sects do, so is point doesn't make sense) has emerged or overtaken the Sect&quot;. The Tzimisce as the defacto diarchs of the Sect along with the Lasombra (pre-V5 atleast), definitely wouldn't allow this to happen.<br /> <br /> Even if we accept a fissure of an &quot;all-same-clan&quot; Packs among the Sabbat, they'd be exceedingly rare and definitely not comprise the mass defection we saw in V5. I notioned this way back ages ago in many other threads and probably this one too, I still don't buy the Elders of the Lasombra defecting toward the Camarilla. It just doesn't make any sense considering their attitudes and how they shaped all their pride into the Sabbat. The other fiat that V5 writing also seemingly ignores is the Beckoning and to what extent and even how the Elders could coordinate stuff with a massive upheaval leave from the Sabbat, all in the midst of the &quot;wars going on in the Middle-East&quot;. You're telling me Anchillae and Neonate Lasombra orchestrated all of this? Please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:05:19-07:00","id":1444887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444886#post1444886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many centuries has the Sabbat run for up to this point, and with along that, the Vinculum one of the main components on why it remained together? The whole point of it in the first place was to prohibit the car crash scenario that is the Lasombra &quot;mass defection&quot;. And the Sabbat within itself wouldn't be stupid to allow the majority of the Lasombra to have Vaulderie only done among their own clan only, barring inferences toward a theory that since &quot;no monoculture of the Sabbat (the Sabbat certainly DOES have a culture, all the Sects do, so is point doesn't make snese) has emerged or overtaken the Sect&quot;. The Tzimisce as the defacto diarchs of the Sect along with the Lasombra (pre-V5 atleast), definitely wouldn't allow this to happen.<br /> <br /> Even if we accept a fissure of an &quot;all-same-clan&quot; Packs among the Sabbat, they'd be exceedingly rare and definitely not comprise the mass defection we saw in V5. I notioned this way back ages ago in many other threads and probably this one too, I still don't buy the Elders of the Lasombra defecting toward the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vinculum has never kept the Sabbat together. The IDEOLOGY of the Sabbat is what keeps the Sabbat together. I think the bloody brutal history of the Sabbat makes it clear that the Vinculum doesn't prevent any civil strife among the Sabbat and is not nearly the panacea that people claim it is. It also is a very &quot;video game&quot; sort of solution. &quot;Oh the Sabbat would never have any defectors because the Sabbat are all Blood Bound to one another!&quot;<br /> <br /> Which doesn't reflect the lore or the setting and isn't particularly interesting as a character trait either. We've already had an entire city of Lasombra defect in the past as well.<br /> <br /> As a Sabbat fan, I find it disturbing people would argue that membership in the &quot;other&quot; sect of FreedomTM wouldn't be in the Sabbat because they WANT to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just doesn't make any sense considering their attitudes and how they shaped all their pride into the Sabbat. The other fiat that V5 writing also seemingly ignores is the Beckoning and to what extent and even how the Elders could coordinate stuff a massive upheaval leave from the Sabbat, all in the midst of the &quot;wars going on in the Middle-East&quot;. You're telling me Anchillae and Neonate Lasombra orchestrated all of this? Please. </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a Sabbat fan, I think a split like this was inevitable because I tend to play Antitribu not Lasombra or Tzimisce. The Antitribu have been steadily gaining power in the Sword of Caine for the past few centuries and showing they're not going to be following the leadership of the Keepers regardless. Meredith may have impersonated a Keeper but being a Antitribu was a sign that the shadow's domination was coming to an End.<br /> <br /> I can fully see with the victories on the East Coast and other triumphs that the Lasombra saw their domination coming to an end and decided to have plenty bail.<br /> <br /> Honestly, minus a few hundred Keepers, I think the defection will be good for the Nu Sabbat because they will have a more even membership among the Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:09:08-07:00","id":1444888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444886#post1444886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Sabbat within itself wouldn't be stupid to allow the majority of the Lasombra to have Vaulderie only done among their own clan only, barring inferences toward a theory that since &amp;quot;no monoculture of the Sabbat (the Sabbat certainly DOES have a culture, all the Sects do, so is point doesn't make sense) has emerged or overtaken the Sect&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't misquote me. I never denied that the Sabbat has a culture. I denied that it has a hegemonic monoculture that collectively overrides things like factional strife or Clan allegiance. That's why the Third Sabbat Civil War can mostly be described by what sides different Clans took, not what Sabbat factions did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:12:32-07:00","id":1444891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444888#post1444888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please don't misquote me. I never denied that the Sabbat has a culture. I denied that it has a hegemonic monoculture that collectively overrides things like factional strife or Clan allegiance. That's why the Third Sabbat Civil War can mostly be described by what sides different Clans took, not what Sabbat factions did.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat Civil War in BJD was also described as:<br /> <br /> * Loyalists vs. Traditionalists<br /> * Inquisition vs. Infernalists<br /> * Black Hand vs. True Hand<br /> * Gehenna Warriors vs. No One (no wonder they won)<br /> <br /> BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY:<br /> <br /> 1. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1326497#post1326497\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...97#post1326497</a><br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1326520#post1326520\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...20#post1326520</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:21:07-07:00","id":1444895,"title":"","content":"I never claimed the Vinculum alone was what kept the Sabbat together, it was one of the main components. And yes infighting happened with the Sabbat, but it was never this nonsense we see in V5 with the Lasombra just tail-between-the-legs running to the Camarilla. At all. The Sabbat fought eachother, but always came back together due to many important factors; key being with what you already mentioned, Ideology aswell. <br /> <br /> And yes the, &quot;Oh the Sabbat would never have any defectors because the Sabbat are all Blood Bound to one another!&quot; Is literally a point both in the narrative and in the game mechanic as I already said beforehand. This isn't to imply defections haven't happened or cannot be done, but this sudden and deus-ex-mach approach to shoehorning the Lasombra into the Camarilla is laughable. For the Lasombra defection to work as is with Vinculum as a factor, they should've had other clans of Sabbat Kindred also join them because that's how Packs are supposed to work (broaching on my previous appoint on the idea that &quot;same-clan&quot; Packs would be very rare and not the norm); but no, cleanly and iffily devised, almost ALL are Lasombra that have defected in en masse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:25:39-07:00","id":1444898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444891#post1444891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat Civil War in BJD was also described as:<br /> <br /> * Loyalists vs. Traditionalists<br /> * Inquisition vs. Infernalists<br /> * Black Hand vs. True Hand<br /> * Gehenna Warriors vs. No One (no wonder they won)<br /> <br /> BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY:<br /> <br /> 1. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1326497#post1326497\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...97#post1326497</a><br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1326520#post1326520\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...20#post1326520</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about the one previous, maybe I mixed up the number. Started in New York, lasted about 100 nights, led to recognition of the Panders. Started IIRC when the Brujah antitribu tried to oust the Lasombra from leadership. Seemed to focus a lot on Clan politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:57:35-07:00","id":1444902,"title":"","content":"You know, the Changeling argument does bring up something much more relevant; Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Chimestry used to be the creation of items made of illusory matter. Ravnos used to get all philosophical about the nature of reality and illusion as a result. Now it's obfuscate and thus just a mind trick.<br /> Something really cool went missing because of someone's irrational desire to cut down on possibilities. Chimestry and the Ravnos are now far worse off as a result (Incidentally, obfuscate sucks in V5)<br /> <br /> There was no harm in Obtenebration having it's own realm. Nobody was hurt by it (except the enemies of Lasombra of course). Yet there is harm in deleting it. It should be a no-brainer to keep things as they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:53:06-07:00","id":1444911,"title":"","content":"V5 modus operandi and doctrine is to have everything &quot;Gamified&quot; and &quot;dumbed-down&quot; or &quot;streamlined&quot; like some like to specify it as (like how in the Elder Scroll series so much of the cool background lore or stuff from the successive games gets removed, doesn't show up, or is retconned); instead leaning more to toward the openness and depth just general Tabletop. From the narrative AND mechanics as we've so far seen. I doesn't make sense to me however. VTM (beside the 1st Bloodlines and the formerly being developed 2) isn't about being a video game, its a Tabletop.<br /> <br /> It's the general motion of having a very low expectation of &quot;newcomers&quot; to the franchise with the new Edition; so now everything must be wrought down to piecemeal level with gross general underestimation factor in mind. I literally came onto oWoD from the Bloodlines game alone and from there got hooked in from Wraith of all things, instead of maybe going the predictable route most nu-oWoD fans with maining VTM off the bat, or only ever branching out to the other lines only very later on. The Wraith series alone has troves of lore and other bits, and I still haven't read most of the Wraith books yet aswell.<br /> <br /> Generally like what was discussed in the &quot;V5 vs V20&quot; thread, World of Darkness (atleast the in the Tabletop sense) isn't nowhere near the mainstream to really justify trying to &quot;streamline&quot; the setting. Even if it was in the mainstream, it doesn't deserve all the butchering its gotten of late. Instead of destroying every single aspect or assimilating other things into others, they should be adding on more. And if a new comer has questions about one thing, they can explore the wiki or get the books themselves. The latter would actually help White Wolf since people would be actually purchasing old stuff; and it'd be worthwhile for them to actually get it, since the stuff they want to figure still would have providence in the setting.<br /> <br /> But nope, &quot;STR8ML1NE EVE2YTH1NG!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:55:03-07:00","id":1444912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444902#post1444902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the Changeling argument does bring up something much more relevant; Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Chimestry used to be the creation of items made of illusory matter. Ravnos used to get all philosophical about the nature of reality and illusion as a result. Now it's obfuscate and thus just a mind trick.<br /> Something really cool went missing because of someone's irrational desire to cut down on possibilities. Chimestry and the Ravnos are now far worse off as a result (Incidentally, obfuscate sucks in V5)<br /> <br /> There was no harm in Obtenebration having it's own realm. Nobody was hurt by it (except the enemies of Lasombra of course). Yet there is harm in deleting it. It should be a no-brainer to keep things as they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of the problem with these arguments. The word &quot;harm&quot; is used somewhat subjectively. Some might argue that the vast network of mixups and confusion that result from having three different Abysses, half a dozen Realms of darkness, gets in the way of the story that they might want to tell. Trying to argue that the quality of the entire World of Darkness is tied solely in the parts that resonate with you, in this case convoluted esotericism, seems reductive and self-centered. As someone who *does* like those parts, I don't agree that changing or diminishing them &quot;ruins&quot; the game by any objective standard, because there isn't one.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to a hard answer on whether Dark-Gnosticism or Superheroes-with-Fangs is objectively &quot;better&quot; is which one will be more profitable for Paradox/OPP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:23:37-07:00","id":1444915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">confusion that result from having three different Abysses,</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Abyss the Lasombra interacted with</b>: It was a thing and pseudo-entity that Lasombra literally since they established Obtenebration drew from and communed with. Notice how its a thing here.<br /> <br /> <b>The Abyss mentioned in W:tA</b>: Simply a very dreary and dark laden realm that was some facet of the Middle Umbra. It wasn't a particular entity nor a prison.<br /> <br /> <b>The Abyss mentioned in D:tF</b>: The penultimate place where nu-Wolf apparently is having the Lasombra and Obteneberation somehow be linked to; Despite it being a near impenetrable prison only broken during the events of the Week of Nightmares that had two nukes go off (and it only ever caused a small crack in it, if anything else); it being a place and not an entity onto itself like in the Lasombra clanbook; its explicit purpose being a prison for the Fallen and the Fallen only, so linking Obtenebration / the new &quot;Oblivion&quot; Discipline makes no sense and lorebreaks, because how in the world does the Lasombra draw from a place that's an equivalent a supernatural maximum sentence penitentiary?; and also the mere fact that it breaks Lasombra lore within itself, because how did the initiating establishers of Obtenebration even be able to get out of the Abyss described in Fallen?<br /> <br /> This isn't to poke the fact that the Abyss described in D:tF is literally under Oblivion. If its under Oblivion according to D:tF's own lore strewnage, that it's practically outside reality since the Oblivion is supposed to be the Nil of everything in oWoD. That by itself positions the Abyss in D:tF to not even be associated with the Low Umbra alone. So how and why are the Lasombra suddenly involved with it? And what exact Low Umbric &quot;Abyss&quot; they're drawing power from? (spoiler: they reneged all it due to the &quot;streamline&quot; doctrine, but it all ironically just makes the setting more &quot;convoluted&quot; than before due to not reviewing the setting first and making sensible changes)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:24:51-07:00","id":1444916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444902#post1444902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the Changeling argument does bring up something much more relevant; Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Chimestry used to be the creation of items made of illusory matter. Ravnos used to get all philosophical about the nature of reality and illusion as a result. Now it's obfuscate and thus just a mind trick. Something really cool went missing because of someone's irrational desire to cut down on possibilities. Chimestry and the Ravnos are now far worse off as a result (Incidentally, obfuscate sucks in V5)<br /> <br /> There was no harm in Obtenebration having it's own realm. Nobody was hurt by it (except the enemies of Lasombra of course). Yet there is harm in deleting it. It should be a no-brainer to keep things as they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except barring the Antediluvian, it always was a mind-trick and Auspex already saw through their stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:33:59-07:00","id":1444918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444915#post1444915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Abyss the Lasombra interacted with</b>: It was a thing and pseudo-entity that Lasombra literally since they established Obtenebration drew from and communed with. Notice how its a thing here.<br /> <br /> <b>The Abyss mentioned in W:tA</b>: Simply a very dreary and dark laden realm that was some facet of the Middle Umbra. It wasn't a particular entity nor a prison.<br /> <br /> <b>The Abyss mentioned in D:tF</b>: The penultimate place where nu-Wolf apparently is having the Lasombra and Obteneberation somehow be linked to; Despite it being a near impenetrable prison only broken during the events of the Week of Nightmares that had two nukes go off (and it only ever caused a small crack in it, if anything else); it being a place and not an entity onto itself like in the Lasombra clanbook; its explicit purpose being a prison for the Fallen and the Fallen only, so linking Obtenebration / the new &amp;quot;Oblivion&amp;quot; Discipline makes no sense and lorebreaks, because how in the world does the Lasombra draw from a place that's an equivalent a supernatural maximum sentence penitentiary?; and also the mere fact that it breaks Lasombra lore within itself, because how did the initiating establishers of Obtenebration even be able to get out of the Abyss described in Fallen?<br /> <br /> This isn't to poke the fact that the Abyss described in D:tF is literally under Oblivion. If its under Oblivion according to D:tF's own lore strewnage, that it's practically outside reality since the Oblivion is supposed to be the Nil of everything in oWoD. That by itself positions the Abyss in D:tF to not even be associated with the Low Umbra alone. So how and why are the Lasombra suddenly involved with it? And what exact Low Umbric &amp;quot;Abyss&amp;quot; they're drawing power from? (spoiler: they reneged all it due to the &amp;quot;streamline&amp;quot; doctrine, but it all ironically just makes the setting more &amp;quot;convoluted&amp;quot; than before due to not reviewing the setting first and making sensible changes)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I don't know why you quoted me when the details of the three different Abysses were pretty much completely completely irrelevant to what I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that &quot;The World of Darkness is objectively worse because of X cosmology change&quot; is a nonsense statement because there is no objective answer to which subjective opinion or playstyle is &quot;right&quot; or &quot;better.&quot;<br /> <br /> You may not like the types of stories being told, but there is no objective argument to prove your side more or less right than, for example, CTPhipps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:37:58-07:00","id":1444919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444895#post1444895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never claimed the Vinculum alone was what kept the Sabbat together, it was one of the main components. And yes infighting happened with the Sabbat, but it was never this nonsense we see in V5 with the Lasombra just tail-between-the-legs running to the Camarilla. At all. The Sabbat fought eachother, but always came back together due to many important factors; key being with what you already mentioned, Ideology aswell.<br /> <br /> And yes the, &quot;Oh the Sabbat would never have any defectors because the Sabbat are all Blood Bound to one another!&quot; Is literally a point both in the narrative and in the game mechanic as I already said beforehand. This isn't to imply defections haven't happened or cannot be done, but this sudden and deus-ex-mach approach to shoehorning the Lasombra into the Camarilla is laughable. For the Lasombra defection to work as is with Vinculum as a factor, they should've had other clans of Sabbat Kindred also join them because that's how Packs are supposed to work (broaching on my previous appoint on the idea that &quot;same-clan&quot; Packs would be very rare and not the norm); but no, cleanly and iffily devised, almost ALL are Lasombra that have defected in en masse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the significantly much more easier thing is that the Amis Noctis manipulated it behind the scenes so the other Lasombra were transferred away for a couple of months. The Vinculum's biggest weakness is that it lasts a couple of months without being refueled.<br /> <br /> Really, you could actually force a defection by having the initial defectors force the other Lasombra to share the Vinculum with them over their fellow Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:38:11-07:00","id":1444920,"title":"","content":"How &quot;mass&quot; really is the defection though? The lasombra are allowed very small numbers in chicago. Other cities probably accept even less. Maybe a couple hundred?<br /> <br /> I expect more defections come from lasombra who go to the middle east and their entire pack gets destroyed and so the wonder around lost for a bit before hearing a out the defection option then making plans to take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:39:32-07:00","id":1444921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444920#post1444920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How &quot;mass&quot; really is the defection though? The lasombra are allowed very small numbers in chicago. Other cities probably accept even less. Maybe a couple hundred?<br /> <br /> I expect more defections come from lasombra who go to the middle east and their entire pack gets destroyed and so the wonder around lost for a bit before hearing a out the defection option then making plans to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good point. As stated, there's not actually that many vampires in the world. The entire numbers of a Clan in the world are about the number of a small town.<br /> <br /> A few hundred difference is the difference between Antitribu and the mainstream Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:14:11-07:00","id":1444926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;The World of Darkness is objectively worse because of X cosmology change&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> It IS worse since such things degrade the quality of the franchise. If things happen for no reason, with no build up; or if things are nonsensically splattered despite firm precedents otherwise to the contrary, the immersion or taking the setting seriously peters. Especially in a roleplaying game on its own. What if you have a Lasombra from the previous edition and you doing a test run chronicle with only V5 lore background developments in mind? When visiting the Abyss, are you now trapped in it permanently due to it being the nigh-impenetrable prison of the Eloheim? Or are you just cut off from it entirely? What happens now?<br /> <br /> And apparently, which I forgot to bring up, was the fact that (and I literally just seen this off the wiki) the [Lasombra] Antediluvian apparently became one with the Abyss itself? So now with V5 linking the Abyss to the &quot;Low Umbric&quot; version of it, has the Lasombra literally become a prison now? And if we apply retroactivity here (since what has been written for V5 now has done retroactivity by making the Lasombra/Obtenebration linked to the Low Umbric Abyss when it wasn't before), how in the world could [Lasombra] even pull this off; if we're to fully believe that the Abyss is completely inaccessible reality-wise with it being under Oblivion? <br /> <br /> Gratiano apparently killed [Lasombra] during the 1st Anarch Revolts, right? That was in the High-to-Late Middle Ages and certainly was waaay before the Week of Nightmares; there is no way [Lasombra] could've gotten inside (or even the possibly of Obtenebration being developed, but I already talked about that point). Even his article on the wiki says the &quot;Abyssal entities&quot; weren't interested in him because he was former flesh; but in actuality per D:tF's own lore (which of course has been strewn into involvement due to retroactivity), the Fallen would've been VERY interested with [Lasombra] with the fact he seemingly or somehow became their prison; or the fact that he could leave and come back at will, while they were stuck there in torment. <br /> <br /> And with clause of retroactivity; with the correlation of merging Obtenebration and Necromancy into one convenient lazy Discipline called &quot;Oblivion&quot;, and the new implications of the Lasombra now having associative spheres with the Low Umbra; how come there is no new word or plotpoints with discussing the Lasombra having anything to now do with Necromancy or the Low Umbra itself? Will that ever be addressed? Because not any of the Lasombra Clanbooks really at all speak of or did things with the Low Umbra or Necromancy. Everything about it makes no sense or broken in a way that it didn't need to be.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:19:49-07:00","id":1444928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444926#post1444926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It IS worse since such things degrade the quality of the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or improve it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And apparently, which I forgot to bring up, was the fact that (and I literally just seen this off the wiki) the [Lasombra] Antediluvian apparently became one with the Abyss itself? So now with V5 linking the Abyss to the &quot;Low Umbric&quot; version of it, has the Lasombra literally become a prison now? And if we apply retroactivity here (since what has been written for V5 now has done retroactivity by making the Lasombra/Obtenebration linked to the Low Umbric Abyss when it wasn't before), how in the world could [Lasombra] even pull this off; if we're to fully believe that the Abyss is completely inaccessible reality-wise with it being under Oblivion? </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Literally demons have been summoned from the Abyss for millennia. Its why we have demons like Gulfora, Belial, and other Earthbound. Demon: The Fallen made it abundantly clear that infernalist magic was linked to the...infernal, which was imprisoned in the Abyss. It also explains why Moncada was able to remain a devout Catholic while worshiping horrifying things from the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Dude even had True Faith.<br /> <br /> Why? Because he KNEW the reality of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And with clause of retroactivity; with the correlation of merging Obtenebration and Necromancy into one convenient lazy Discipline called &quot;Oblivion&quot;, and the new implications of the Lasombra now having associative spheres with the Low Umbra; how come there is no new word or plotpoints with discussing the Lasombra having anything to now do with Necromancy or the Low Umbra itself? Will that ever be addressed? Because not any of the Lasombra Clanbooks really at all speak of or did things with the Low Umbra or Necromancy. Everything about it makes no sense or broken in a way that it didn't need to be.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Lasombra have been associating with spirits of the Abyss for millennia. Moncada had an enormous demonic monster thing in his Cathedral.<br /> <br /> They also had Abyssal rituals.<br /> <br /> They just weren't contacting regular ghosts. Part of what makes the Discipline merging good and would be even better if they could get more than one rank per Discipline dot leevl is the fact that Kindred powers are a lot more diversified. You no longer are restricted to the powers that were the same for every level but have a huge amount more flexibility.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:37:37-07:00","id":1444935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, the significantly much more easier thing is that the Amis Noctis manipulated it behind the scenes so the other Lasombra were transferred away for a couple of months. The Vinculum's biggest weakness is that it lasts a couple of months without being refueled.<br /> <br /> Really, you could actually force a defection by having the initial defectors force the other Lasombra to share the Vinculum with them over their fellow Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>Umm per the books...no Vincs never fade. Thats right in the mechanics of the Vaulderie. V20 Page 290<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike normal blood bonds, Vinculi do not fade over time \u2014 a Vinculum left after a Vaulderie with a vampire in nights hundreds of years past is still as potent as the night it arose. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:38:59-07:00","id":1444938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444935#post1444935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm per the books...no Vincs never fade. Thats right in the mechanics of the Vaulderie. V20 Page 290<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, I thought that the Vinculum was much weaker.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> I believe I was confused because Vinculum can and do get altered in the LEVEL of their devotion with each subsequent Vinculum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:48:55-07:00","id":1444940,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the easiest fix for Lasombra in the Camarilla would have been just to do the following... &quot;with the Sabbat all distracted by the Gehenna War and their losses limiting their ability to retaliate against them as they once did, the Lasombra antritribu elders decide now is the time to step out of the shadows and make a play for a seat on the Council that was recently stripped from the Brujah... including a reminder that they've been loyal to the Camarilla from the start, having sided against their errant kin who joined the Sabbat, and remain loyal even now.<br /> <br /> Once they get the seat at the table and no longer need to hide their lineage, suddenly every city has a few Kindred &quot;come out&quot; as Lasombra because it turns out the Antitribu have been part of the Camarilla the entire time. They're just done hiding their numbers and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:51:31-07:00","id":1444942,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I think defecting Sabbat have really interesting story lines. I really like the way LA by Night handled it where the Sabbat are genuinely TERRIFYING to the Anarchs and it shows the difference between them and &quot;regular&quot; vampires.<br /> <br /> But yes, I tend to think the Antitribu were underdone in all of this.<br /> <br /> What was Montano's role in the defection, if any? Has he been Beckoned? This could have been its own story. Well, beyond THE SACRIFICE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:14:04-07:00","id":1444950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gulfora, Belial, and other Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gulfora as per her wiki page describes, is described as a &quot;succubus&quot;. She certainly has nothing to do with the Fallen and she is inhabiting her own body. She definitely was never trapped in or associated with the Abyss. And looking at the source where this character comes from, she comes from Chicago: By Night, 2nd edition; this poor character with the logic of D:tF is probably retroactively (I've been saying this too much, bleh) retconned with how D:tF sets up Demons. The only one who remained in &quot;humanoid/human&quot; form with their own body post &quot;God&quot; shipping all the Fallen into the D:tF Abyss was Lucifer, and no one else. She also definitely couldn't be a post-Week of Nightmare escaped Fallen for how long she has been active.<br /> <br /> Your Earthbound point: Yes, the Earthbound as per D:tF's &quot;amazing&quot; lore were more or less were such strong entities, that they couldn't inhabit mortal bodies, only objects; with this turning into D:tF's biggest blunder of &quot;heheheheh, all the Pagan religions are actually categorically false and nondescript in oWoD/D:tF's framing, because each one is actually a pawn/proxy for the Earthbound; and Lucifer made Christianity to combat them, so essentially with how Lucifer inaugurated Christianity from the shadows and D:tF's lore, the Book of Gensis basically becomes the main focal origin point of oWoD now, hurrrrrr durrrrr&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your other point about &quot;summoning&quot; ends up in a dead end aswell. Yes, its true that the Lasombra called upon and rightly summoned the shadows of the Abyss (VTM version) through the naturality of their skill in Obtenebration. But notice how these things summoned WEREN'T Earthbound nor any Fallen at all.<br /> <br /> If we went with your logic: apparently now the Lasombra would be somesort of Earthbound whisperers; y'know, being able to somehow muster the power to temporarily break an Earthbound out the (D:tF, impenetrable prison) Abyss of all things, just for a simple fight in the alley against enemy Camarilla. And lets also ignore the fact that each Earthbound as described in D:tF is a highly intelligent, but malevolent Being that is now somehow being directly manipulated by some rando Lasombra Neonate in a theoretical tangent of thought. Or the fact that the (VTM) Abyss merely only had a pseudo-intellect and ostensibly had nothing as described in likes to the Earthbound... Sounds about right.. right?<br /> <br /> Not to even remind that the whole main plotpoint surrounding Earthbound is that they must inhabit objects to even be viable in &quot;real&quot; reality, but suddenly Lasombra all around the globe utilizing Obtenebration summon them in and out the Abyss so easily? Wut?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Lasombra have been associating with <b>spirits</b> of the Abyss for millennia. Moncada had an enormous demonic monster thing in his Cathedral.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Yes, but they weren't the Fallen at all however. Nor would the Lasombra be able to have any interaction with them anyway, with how the (D:tF) Abyss worked. At all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They just weren't contacting regular ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where have I inferred this? One of my actual main contentions in the first place was that they're being associated with the Low Umbra to begin with. What the Lasombra communed with were always mostlikely ephemeric dark spirits of the Middle Umbra or something onto itself. But certainly not anything to do with the Low Umbra. Wraiths =/= Spirits. Even the books make it certain that Spirits do not like Wraiths.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Part of what makes the Discipline merging good and would be even better if they could get more than one rank per Discipline dot leevl is the fact that Kindred powers are a lot more diversified.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Merging Disciplines, especially ones that have no connection or much correlation is never good. It breaks certain niches or makes the game more staleness with sameness. And part of their modus operandi for this new Edition with their &quot;streamline&quot; of mechanics has been to remove more powers per dot to begin with. The funny thing is if I remember now; haven't they literally just made the Lasombra and the so-called &quot;Hecata&quot; clan both have the Discipline called &quot;Oblivon&quot;, but literally gave them different power sets? WTF, why remove Obtenebration and Necromancy then? Why give it the same name, but different powers altogether? Everything about these developments have panned out horribly so far.<br /> <br /> Nothing about this has been an improvement. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:25:16-07:00","id":1444951,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's a reference to the Earthbound being freed from the Abyss:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Belial_(DTF\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Belial_(DTF</a>)<br /> <br /> <i><b>When the Fallen were imprisoned in the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Abyss_(DTF)\" target=\"_blank\">Abyss</a>, Belial was the one most affected by Lucifer's disappearance. </b>His former love for the Lightbringer transformed into violent hatred and self-loathing that were only aggrandized by the aeons of imprisonment. <b>When Lucifer managed to plant the seeds of summoning into the minds of mortals, Belial was summoned by the court magicians of the Shang Dynasty in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/China_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">China</a>, with offerings of jade, silk and thousand immolated bodies.</b> If he had been to join Lucifer in the crusade to wrest Heaven from God, then the Apocalypse would have been no more than a handful of years away. Fortunately for the sake of humanity and all Creation, Belial is obsessed with his hatred of Lucifer, and cares far more about finding and destroying his former lord and master than for anything else, even usurping the throne of Heaven. In order to destroy the Morningstar and claim his power, Belial would give up mastery of all Creation, or indeed reduce Creation to ashes. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:10:19-07:00","id":1444962,"title":"","content":"Yes, I already saw that blurb when I checked the wiki for Belial himself when you mentioned him previously, and I already addressed the aspect of the summoning part itself. It still doesn't match up nor does the blurb address my points or inductions. The D:tF Abyss as is was a prison of pure blandness and falterhood entirely. It had no &quot;infernal&quot; magic(k) anything and the Lasombra didn't draw their power from there previously at all, barring the V5 retrocons of today. It's supposed be a prison, not a theme park. Nor is there any logic to inference that the Lasombra are somehow Fallen whisperers of a sort and the shadows they've manipulated for so long; are actually the whole time some manner of Fallen that can freely phase in and out of the Abyss with the orchestration of the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> You also forget the fact that every Fallen is a fully sentient-entity, and not the pseudo-intelligence that was(/is?) described with things the Lasombra interacted if. If your point about the former were true, then as soon as the Lasombra were to ever use Obtenebration (and that means every single one using Obtenebration across the globe in the setting of oWoD); the entirety of the Abyss as described in D:tF would be entirely empty; because there is no way in hell (pun intended) any Fallen would agree to being sent back to Abyss nor would they even dine to probably obey the Lasombra after getting a proverbial &quot;get out of jail free card&quot;.<br /> <br /> So these things would happen with the applied logic of the (D:tF) Abyss being the faux of the Lasombra's Obtenebration all this time:<br /> <br /> 1. The Abyss would be entirely empty. All of the Fallen are out now and have possessed bodies throughout the globe.<br /> <br /> 2. The Lasombra lose half their abilities in Obtenebration; some techniques still work, but the majority of what they could do before is now gone with the Abyss &quot;drying up&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3. The Lasombra would've been even probably with the Sabbat (Preempt Edit: certainly, because they'd be tagged as infernalists) along with the Camarilla would massively blood hunt the Lasombra for being huge Masquerade breaches for causing a Demon semi-apocalypse; it'd be akin to what happened to the Salubri.<br /> <br /> 4. The entire globe goes into Bedlam, because some Fallen more than others have gone crazy/couldn't endure the intrinsic entropic banalness of the Abyss; so now a whole plot event would have to be written to address that: Does the Technocracy gets involved like what happened with [Ravnos]? How do the Garou react to this, sign of the Wyrm being ascendant? How do the few rational minded Fallen even try to survive this world?<br /> <br /> 5. Tiering into Mage, how would the entire Consensus dynamic change with the mass of humanity seeing the outright supernatural with their own eyes; with so many Demons inside humans doing ostensibly supernatural things with their Lores/basic Enhanced physiologies? Would the Traditions / Crafts become more stronger due to this, along with the Technocracy weakening?<br /> <br /> 6. And what of the Wan Kuei. How would THEY react? Or even the Yama Kings?<br /> <br /> This is why the Lasombra being retrofitted toward the Low Umbra sphere and further into having their former Abyss pre-V5, now encompass the (D:tF) Abyss makes no sense. Too lorebreaky and narrative is zig-tagged around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-20-2021, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:25:25-07:00","id":1444967,"title":"","content":"Allow me to rebuttal that with one sentence, &quot;Except you have given no reason why Obternation would free the Demons because there's nothing that says that it permanently frees them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obternation reaches into the Abyss and pulls out Stygian darkness from the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Anti-Existence if you will.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can communicate with the Demons therein.<br /> <br /> What it DOESN'T do is free demons and provide them bodies. As we see with the Earthbound and infernalism, even if you summon a demon, they're eventually drawn back into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The only reason they aren't is after the prison is cracked or they have a specially crafted totem made for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachme