:"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T22:28:39-07:00","id":1444994,"title":"","content":"Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> , should have taken your earlier recommendation.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Vaulderie, do you see that as a practice the Lasombra might potentially continue to practice even as members of the Camarilla? IIRC it was in LotC that a Sabbat infiltrator was (possibly?) picked up on by a Malkavian in the intro fiction to their chapter because he noticed the infiltrator's willingness to drink vitae without fearing a blood bond. It's a practice that could retain tactical value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T22:42:40-07:00","id":1444997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444994#post1444994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> , should have taken your earlier recommendation.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Vaulderie, do you see that as a practice the Lasombra might potentially continue to practice even as members of the Camarilla? IIRC it was in LotC that a Sabbat infiltrator was (possibly?) picked up on by a Malkavian in the intro fiction to their chapter because he noticed the infiltrator's willingness to drink vitae without fearing a blood bond. It's a practice that could retain tactical value.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some Anarchs that have taken to it as of Anarchs Unbound and I suspect we'll find the practice has grown with other defecting Sabbat. The real question is whether the Vaulderie is a benefit or a hindrance in this time period.<br /> <br /> It ends the Blood Bond but the lesser version of it is still impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T02:44:19-08:00","id":1498745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444950#post1444950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gulfora as per her wiki page describes, is described as a &quot;succubus&quot;. She certainly has nothing to do with the Fallen and she is inhabiting her own body. She definitely was never trapped in or associated with the Abyss. And looking at the source where this character comes from, she comes from Chicago: By Night, 2nd edition; this poor character with the logic of D:tF is probably retroactively (I've been saying this too much, bleh) retconned with how D:tF sets up Demons. The only one who remained in &quot;humanoid/human&quot; form with their own body post &quot;God&quot; shipping all the Fallen into the D:tF Abyss was Lucifer, and no one else. She also definitely couldn't be a post-Week of Nightmare escaped Fallen for how long she has been active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little WW Wiki nitpick - Gulfora actually comes from Chicago: By Night, <b>1st </b>edition, not 2nd.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the matter of what Gulfora actually <b>is</b> can be considered sketchy at best, but fluff (she's outright stated to be an unreliable narrator by nature) or crunch-wise - if there's some consistent about her, is her abilties NOT fitting with how demons are supposed to work, no matter the edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Plus, depending on how one interprets the &quot;<i>when God created the beings of the sea and air</i>&quot; claim of hers, she might some sort of intelligent pre-human beast, nature spirit or elemental instead, specially when considered alongside the &quot;She is also unaffected by the sun or fire but avoids both.&quot; blurb in her notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1444993#post1444993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">La la la lasombra...<br /> <br /> I'll show myself out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And now i can't stop myself of mixing that with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NakTu_VZxJ0\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-04-2022, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T05:59:06-08:00","id":1498755,"title":"","content":"The biggest objection I can comment on with the Abyss now being oblivion is that it's thematically less interesting. The creepy ambiguity of what exactly obtenerbration was was a feature not a big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T08:16:19-08:00","id":1498763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498755#post1498755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest objection I can comment on with the Abyss now being oblivion is that it's thematically less interesting. The creepy ambiguity of what exactly obtenerbration was was a feature not a big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly<br /> Was the Abyss just another little pocket realm in the umbra, an ancient prison, or truly a realm outside creation entirely unamicable to reality? Your entire story could revolve around the abyss. It was a mystery, hence we call students &quot;Mystics&quot; because, y'know, they're involved in mysteries. (as opposed to thaumaturges who all believe they know almost exactly what they're doing)<br /> <br /> That and, y'know, I'm pretty convinced that V5 arrived at the wrong answer. Lasombra never had anything to do with ghosts before and Oblivion from the underworld aught to be far more corrosive. It's a little frustrating to see someone who's not only really wrong but also really smug about the perceived cleverness of their answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T09:07:29-08:00","id":1498768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498763#post1498763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly<br /> Was the Abyss just another little pocket realm in the umbra, an ancient prison, or truly a realm outside creation entirely unamicable to reality? Your entire story could revolve around the abyss. It was a mystery, hence we call students &quot;Mystics&quot; because, y'know, they're involved in mysteries. (as opposed to thaumaturges who all believe they know almost exactly what they're doing)</div> </div> </div> </div>Terms like &quot;mystic&quot;, &quot;student&quot;, &quot;lorekeeper&quot;, &quot;sage&quot;, &quot;expert&quot; or &quot;occultist&quot; can also be drawn and established mainly in regard to social norms or practicalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T10:27:02-08:00","id":1498778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498768#post1498768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terms like &quot;mystic&quot;, &quot;student&quot;, &quot;lorekeeper&quot;, &quot;sage&quot;, &quot;expert&quot; or &quot;occultist&quot; can also be drawn and established mainly in regard to social norms or practicalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't make sense of this. Could you rephrase that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:42:17-08:00","id":1498783,"title":"","content":"Also, did Talley really kill Lucita or shall she be Regent?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m in the camp that Talley and Lucita have some sort of deal and she didn\u2019t suffer final death at all.<br /> <br /> Here ya go!<br /> [/QUOTE]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T13:18:01-08:00","id":1498793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498783#post1498783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, did Talley really kill Lucita or shall she be Regent?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m in the camp that Talley and Lucita have some sort of deal and she didn\u2019t suffer final death at all.<br /> <br /> Here ya go!</div> </div> </div> </div>My inclination is that Lucita was the last attempt by the Sabbat with any semblance of sanity to hold onto an organized sect. When she saw what was happening, she faked her death and bailed.<br /> <br /> Possibly with Anatole lecturing her on what an incredibly stupid idea joining the Sword of Caine was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:19:57-08:00","id":1498797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498745#post1498745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little WW Wiki nitpick - Gulfora actually comes from Chicago: By Night, <b>1st </b>edition, not 2nd.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the matter of what Gulfora actually <b>is</b> can be considered sketchy at best, but fluff (she's outright stated to be an unreliable narrator by nature) or crunch-wise - if there's some consistent about her, is her abilties NOT fitting with how demons are supposed to work, no matter the edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Plus, depending on how one interprets the &quot;<i>when God created the beings of the sea and air</i>&quot; claim of hers, she might some sort of intelligent pre-human beast, nature spirit or elemental instead, specially when considered alongside the &quot;She is also unaffected by the sun or fire but avoids both.&quot; blurb in her notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And now i can't stop myself of mixing that with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NakTu_VZxJ0\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Side note: I like how you cane see her parents' influence, but she is still doing her own thing. Also, Wednesday almost seems to be in an ecstatic state there. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:33:25-08:00","id":1498798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498793#post1498793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My inclination is that Lucita was the last attempt by the Sabbat with any semblance of sanity to hold onto an organized sect. When she saw what was happening, she faked her death and bailed.<br /> <br /> Possibly with Anatole lecturing her on what an incredibly stupid idea joining the Sword of Caine was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, i always felt having her candidacy for Regent was a bit of nonsense that could only be topped in ridiculousness by someone suggesting Montano instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:45:35-08:00","id":1498802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498798#post1498798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, i always felt having her candidacy for Regent was a bit of nonsense that could only be topped in ridiculousness by someone suggesting Montano instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is that being the Regent is something only a complete outsider to Sabbat power will achieve because like the Princedom vs. Primogen, the smarter Elders know it's better to be a Cardinal or Pricius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-04-2022, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T15:20:42-08:00","id":1498804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498802#post1498802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My view is that being the Regent is something only a complete outside to Sabbat power will achieve because like the Princedom vs. Primogen, the smarter Elders know it's better to be a Cardinal or Pricius.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what you have less smart, more egocentric, fanatic or unstable elders or ancilla to aim for. Bonfire of vanities is a thing even for centuries old supernaturally preserved corpses.<br /> <br /> And that without going into a number of Antitribu or the Panders taking a shot at the title for these or other personal and rational reasons of their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Plus Lucita is one of the most active Lasombra Antitribu around, centuries-long nemesis of, until very recently, a major spiritual leader of her clan whom she destroyed (that also happened to be her estranged sire) and for a time involved enough with the Camarilla to have a stint as an archon druing and after the Convention of Thorns - under Harderstadt, of all people, to boot!<br /> <br /> Her standing in relation to the Sabbat in general and clan Lasombra in particular seems to go <b><i>a little </i></b>beyond merely &quot;an outsider&quot;.... Just sayin'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-05-2022, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T02:45:01-08:00","id":1498829,"title":"","content":"Mostly I got the Impression she joined the Sabbat because lasombra were a Sabbat clan and someone at white wolf felt the Signature pcs should reflect their sect. Realistically they should have just made another lasombra like they did with the gangrel and becket.<br /> <br /> On a practical level lucita is currently illusive is probably still Sabbat because v5 can't really replicate her raw power and path membership from previous editions. V5 sabbat was pretending path of night was path of cathari as I recall.<br /> <br /> They could probably have her 'run' for Regent now. The sects frankly a bit of a joke in v5 in terms of organization so as long as you're violent enough the only issue if you can get enough of the priscus council behind and kill any other 'regents'. It could even be an easy out if white wolf want to soft retcon the sect to a revised/v20 style group again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-05-2022, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T03:39:22-08:00","id":1498831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498829#post1498829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I got the Impression she joined the Sabbat because lasombra were a Sabbat clan and someone at white wolf felt the Signature pcs should reflect their sect. Realistically they should have just made another lasombra like they did with the gangrel and becket.<br /> <br /> On a practical level lucita is currently illusive is probably still Sabbat because v5 can't really replicate her raw power and path membership from previous editions. V5 sabbat was pretending path of night was path of cathari as I recall.<br /> <br /> They could probably have her 'run' for Regent now. The sects frankly a bit of a joke in v5 in terms of organization so as long as you're violent enough the only issue if you can get enough of the priscus council behind and kill any other 'regents'. It could even be an easy out if white wolf want to soft retcon the sect to a revised/v20 style group again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it was a terrible idea to make her Sabbat and ruined her character.<br /> <br /> I really wish they would end that experiment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T04:30:40-08:00","id":1498834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498831#post1498831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it was a terrible idea to make her Sabbat and ruined her character.<br /> <br /> I really wish they would end that experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, I love a good Greek tragedy and lucitas fall from grace covers that nicely. Her efforts to defy monconda ensured she did what he wanted. Its not what I'd have done but I can appreciate it.<br /> <br /> V5 I'd probably have her make a power play for regent autarkis or the instigator of the lasombra defection if we're going to make a purse out of pig skin. She's actually pretty vile even outside of the Sabbat so theirs a degree of toxic shitty behavoir which makes anything easy to justify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-05-2022, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T05:25:13-08:00","id":1498838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498834#post1498834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, I love a good Greek tragedy and lucitas fall from grace covers that nicely. Her efforts to defy monconda ensured she did what he wanted. Its not what I'd have done but I can appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except therer's not much of a buildup or sense of perspective on why the hell would she make such a choice in the first place - centuries of opposing the sect suddenly means nothing because Mon\u00e7ada is finally a goner, by her hand to boot? Honestly never saw what was supposed to be the logic, rational, emotional or otherwise on that.<br /> <br /> Damn, her as the one jumpstarting a mass defection of Lasombra in parallel to her final tango against her sire would probably have worked much better, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T06:05:56-08:00","id":1498841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498745#post1498745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little WW Wiki nitpick - Gulfora actually comes from Chicago: By Night, <b>1st </b>edition, not 2nd.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the matter of what Gulfora actually <b>is</b> can be considered sketchy at best, but fluff (she's outright stated to be an unreliable narrator by nature) or crunch-wise - if there's some consistent about her, is her abilties NOT fitting with how demons are supposed to work, no matter the edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there was an intention to have succubi as a unique type of creature at some point, but this was never really handled consistently.<br /> <br /> STGttS, for instance, also gives a description of another succubus, Lucrecia, which is not too dissimilar to Gulfura. <br /> <br /> Unlike Gulfora, it isn't expressly stated whether Lucrecia occupies her own body or inhabits a mortal vessel, but she can teleport, which I assume is a rough approximation of Gulfura's ability to turn insubstantial using the system of Investments in that book. She also does the usual succubus things of feeding from sex, although this succubus has also learned how to blood bond vampires.<br /> <br /> Also in that section of the book is a Scottish demon that lives off cat sacrifices, which is about as far from the Elohim as lupines are from Kindred. <br /> <br /> It seems like the intent in early WoD books is that &quot;demon&quot; is a subjective category, covering various minor gods and spirits that don't fit into other splats.<br /> <br /> This approach appears into other Sabbat books (e.g., The Chaos Factor and Mexico City by Night) which also have polytheistic gods and nature spirits working like demons who can grant Investments or teach powers. So I think they're definitely separate from the Elohim, on the whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, depending on how one interprets the &quot;<i>when God created the beings of the sea and air</i>&quot; claim of hers, she might some sort of intelligent pre-human beast, nature spirit or elemental instead, specially when considered alongside the &quot;She is also unaffected by the sun or fire but avoids both.&quot; blurb in her notes. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, she could be some sort of Umbrood, a leftover bygone or even a fae being (maybe an Inanimae, Lycian or ancient Thallain). Gulfura's write up suggests either a Fallen (&quot;created along with the other angels, and fell from grace&quot;) or an Inanimae/Umbrood (&quot;malevolent force of nature&quot;). I could see her being a djinn from CTD, too.<br /> <br /> I rather like the vaguer demons of the older books. But I think even DTF doesn't negate the role of various other spirits as being demons. <br /> <br /> It's just that the Elohim see all other spirits through a Christian lens, just as the changelings see other supernaturals as &quot;Prodigals&quot; who've forgotten they're faeries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-08-2022, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T07:20:20-08:00","id":1498851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498778#post1498778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't make sense of this. Could you rephrase that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that honorifics or titles used by a particular group or organization - rather than chosen through a process of careful selection according to a particular group's beliefs, ideas, concepts, or goals - could be decided upon according nearly entirely to social norms or practical details. The former seems to be more common in World of Darkness, but I am sure that there are surely some teams or organizations that go by names and titles selected through rather mundane criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T10:47:59-08:00","id":1498872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498841#post1498841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there was an intention to have succubi as a unique type of creature at some point, but this was never really handled consistently.<br /> <br /> STGttS, for instance, also gives a description of another succubus, Lucrecia, which is not too dissimilar to Gulfura.<br /> <br /> Unlike Gulfora, it isn't expressly stated whether Lucrecia occupies her own body or inhabits a mortal vessel, but she can teleport, which I assume is a rough approximation of Gulfura's ability to turn insubstantial using the system of Investments in that book. She also does the usual succubus things of feeding in sex, although this succubus has also learned how to blood bond vampires.<br /> <br /> Also in that section of the book is a Scottish demon that lives off cat sacrifices, which is about as far from the Elohim as lupines are from Kindred.<br /> <br /> It seems like the intent in early WoD books is that &quot;demon&quot; is a subjective category, covering various minor gods and spirits that don't fit into other splats.<br /> <br /> This approach appears into other Sabbat books (e.g., The Chaos Factor and Mexico City by Night) which also have polytheistic gods and nature spirits working like demons who can grant Investments or teach powers. So I think they're definitely separate from the Elohim, on the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say it's more of a backwards compatibility issue.<br /> <br /> STGttS provided us with a system for demons, pacts and related things with a clear <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lesser_Key_of_Solomon#Ars_Goetia\" target=\"_blank\">goetic</a>/medieval demonology flair (as shown by Barliagus' title/type, the Cataboligne - damn, many of their names have a medieval renaissance italy vibe to it) but also riffing from kindred mechanics for ST convenience.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Werewolf. instead of &quot;patching&quot; things by representing spirits with gifts, atributes and skills, prefered emphasize their &quot;otherness&quot; as immaterial beings and giving a set of connected but separate mechanics of their own. One that Mage would <b>also </b>adopt for convenience out of consistency and due to its versatility. It's also in Mage's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Book_of_Madness\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Madness</a> where the subject of demons as perhaps a label for a variety of beings that might or not relate to goetic or biblical mythologies is brought into the open, i think.<br /> <br /> Masquerade kind of becomes the odd man out in that it just sits on the whole &quot;using the old or adopting the new&quot; issue (as usual across too many editions...) and act like it doesn't even exist.<br /> <br /> THEN comes DtF with the Elohim/Fallen as a player option and allegedly THE OG rebellious angels exiled from heaven into hell/the Abyss for ages. (What is on itself sketchy like f##k when one considers that the idea of a host of angels rebelling against the Creator is a very late construction in biblical mythology - and possibly related to zoroastric influences during the hebrew's exile period, but i digress)<br /> <br /> <br /> Gulfora is something from <b>so much before </b>all of those editions and cross-splat retcons it's kind of hilarious the more you read on her on her own terms.<br /> Like the fact her Dominate 5 affects only men (gender preferences notwithstanding) what should include possession while her Presence suffers no such issue, the &quot;<i>feeding</i>&quot; through sex bit, her blood being useless to kindred and vice-versa among other little things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bezariel\" target=\"_blank\">Bezariel,&quot;the Blood Angel&quot;</a> from Rage Across Russia can be seen as an even more hilarious case of this, in that, even though the original was clearly made with an &quot;alien deep umbral spirit claiming to be an angel&quot; (maybe - i'm not even sure he does claim to or if it was the mad mage who summoned it in Baba Yaga's service) lens in mind, someone would try to make him into a sample <b>Earthbound</b>.<br /> <br /> The entity who was fascinated by people on Earth having easy access to <b>glass spheres</b>, because they were immensely valuable for him - and hard to come by wherever it comes from. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-05-2022, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T11:26:15-08:00","id":1498875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498851#post1498851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that honorifics or titles used by a particular group or organization - rather than chosen through a process of careful selection according to a particular group's beliefs, ideas, concepts, or goals - could be decided upon according nearly entirely to social norms or practical details. The former seems to be more common in World of Darkness, but I am sure that there are surely some teams or organizations that go by names and titles selected through rather mundane criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean some people think wizard and sorcerer mean the exact same thing without any different connotations and thus it's entirely possible that &quot;mystics&quot; was an arbitrary choice? <br /> Unlikely. Literally every other pre-v5 magical group in VTM has picked appropriate names for themselves, it'd be weird if Mystics was an arbitration. The only stickler is maybe &quot;necromancer&quot; if we go by strict &quot;What the latin means&quot; conventions and even then, half the more common necromancy powers fit within that definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T21:45:02-08:00","id":1498910,"title":"","content":"Was reflecting on the thread and I think the reason v5 lasombra are almost unrecognizable is because v5 thematically doesn't really suit the clan at all.<br /> <br /> - The lasombra are a very setting specific clan with strong cultural aspects.<br /> <br /> -lasombra embrace vampirism with zeal.<br /> <br /> -lasombra had a unique discipline with elderich horror subtext.<br /> <br /> V5 as a setting where you're expected to lean into humanity and clans are bassically character class intrinsically doesn't work for lasombra. Which is why v5 representation is almost a different clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T01:50:14-08:00","id":1498925,"title":"","content":"Most Clan description in V5 are largely similar to earlier editions, I don't see this drift towards &quot;Clans-as-character-classes&quot;: Lasombra weren't also particularly changed in their general depiction, they've had a political realigning but they still are a Church-connected Clan of social darwinists with a horror discipline (the eldritch element is perhaps less overt than what was presented in the Revised Clanbook and in Lore of the Clans, those aspects were moved mostly into the Cult of Shalim).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T06:00:46-08:00","id":1498943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498910#post1498910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was reflecting on the thread and I think the reason v5 lasombra are almost unrecognizable is because v5 thematically doesn't really suit the clan at all.<br /> <br /> - The lasombra are a very setting specific clan with strong cultural aspects.<br /> <br /> -lasombra embrace vampirism with zeal.<br /> <br /> -lasombra had a unique discipline with elderich horror subtext.<br /> <br /> V5 as a setting where you're expected to lean into humanity and clans are bassically character class intrinsically doesn't work for lasombra. Which is why v5 representation is almost a different clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think someone compiled the data for LARP in Vampire: The Masquerade's official fan club and came to the conclusion that Lasombra Antitribu were about the third most commonly played clan after Toreador and Ventrue. Whether or not that's true, they've always been one of the most popular Clans for Camarilla live action players and are hardly lacking in tabletop action as well. Indeed, dating all the way back to the White Wolf forums of the Nineties, I can tell you there were plenty of people who questioned why the Lasombra would be part of the Sabbat and thought they were thematically inconsistent with everything the sect was supposed to be about.<br /> <br /> I've never been one with them but the Lasombra Antitribu have always been massively more prominent in the game than, say, the Tzimisce among the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Enough vampires dying so the Lasombra Antitribu become powerful enough to be their own recognized Clan in the Camarilla was how I initially assumed the events would have gone. Mind you, I'm of the mind that people often dramatically overestimate vampire numbers in terms of these things. How many Lasombra would have to be Embraced/defect to turn the Lasombra Antis into a real clan?<br /> <br /> 100?<br /> <br /> 200?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-06-2022, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T07:15:23-08:00","id":1498948,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Lasombra Antitribu were the largest group of vampires in the Camarilla that didn't have an official seat at the table. There were other groups like the Samedi or the Daughters of Cacophony, but there were very, very few of them. With the fact that both the Gangrel and the Brujah left the Camarilla, by default the Lasombra Antitribu would have basically been able to step up and claim one of those vacant seats. And there was little reason for the Camarilla to deny them since they'd need to give the appearance that the organization was as strong as it ever was.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Lasombra Antitribu only had to embrace a hundred or so vampires, maybe 200 tops, and, boom, there'd probably be about as many of them as there are Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T07:57:08-08:00","id":1498956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498925#post1498925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Clan description in V5 are largely similar to earlier editions, I don't see this drift towards &quot;Clans-as-character-classes&quot;: Lasombra weren't also particularly changed in their general depiction, they've had a political realigning but they still are a Church-connected Clan of social darwinists with a horror discipline (the eldritch element is perhaps less overt than what was presented in the Revised Clanbook and in Lore of the Clans, those aspects were moved mostly into the Cult of Shalim).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is, their's a distinct shift from dread lords of the night to shadowy manipulators (of which their are 12 other clans who go in for shadowy manipulation) more little finger than Tywin, their clan as culture have also been downplayed into the archeotype pc class v5. I'd argue the Elderich element has been replaced with Etherial in v5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498943#post1498943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think someone compiled the data for LARP in Vampire: The Masquerade's official fan club and came to the conclusion that Lasombra Antitribu were about the third most commonly played clan after Toreador and Ventrue. Whether or not that's true, they've always been one of the most popular Clans for Camarilla live action players and are hardly lacking in tabletop action as well. Indeed, dating all the way back to the White Wolf forums of the Nineties, I can tell you there were plenty of people who questioned why the Lasombra would be part of the Sabbat and thought they were thematically inconsistent with everything the sect was supposed to be about.<br /> <br /> I've never been one with them but the Lasombra Antitribu have always been massively more prominent in the game than, say, the Tzimisce among the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Enough vampires dying so the Lasombra Antitribu become powerful enough to be their own recognized Clan in the Camarilla was how I initially assumed the events would have gone. Mind you, I'm of the mind that people often dramatically overestimate vampire numbers in terms of these things. How many Lasombra would have to be Embraced/defect to turn the Lasombra Antis into a real clan?<br /> <br /> 100?<br /> <br /> 200?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are some interesting observations but they don't really come into my main issue . Lasombra are not well suited to V5 as historically presented. Lasombra don't lament their vamparism they consider it a blessing, their horror is elderich and religious v5's is personal, the clan explores alternate moralities which v5 frowns on and social darwinism is bollocks if you're a twitchy screw up with morality pets. this puts them at odds with V5 at a mechanical level. You can formulate an arguement why lasombra would [blank] but that isnt my observation.<br /> <br /> As a side whoever had that take on the Lasombra might as well have argued the Gangrel should be in the Sabbat. That's a terrible take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-06-2022, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T10:03:05-08:00","id":1498967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498956#post1498956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are some interesting observations but they don't really come into my main issue . Lasombra are not well suited to V5 as historically presented. Lasombra don't lament their vamparism they consider it a blessing, their horror is elderich and religious v5's is personal, the clan explores alternate moralities which v5 frowns on and social darwinism is bollocks if you're a twitchy screw up with morality pets. this puts them at odds with V5 at a mechanical level.<br /> <br /> As a side whoever had that take on the Lasombra might as well have argued the Gangrel should be in the Sabbat. That's a terrible take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like this pretty much makes a lot of assumptions about V5 as a playstyle that doesn't seem to be backed up by many of the supplements. V5 goes very hard on the idea that vampires are scumbags and there's not much point in trying to be a &quot;good&quot; one. Instead, it goes with the idea vampires should have SOME redeeming qualities but you are overall an evil person and a psychopath.<br /> <br /> The Humanity system, when done right can be overall extremely alien and vile depending on the Chronicle Tenets and your personal code of ethics.<br /> <br /> Certainly, it allows a lot more flexibility than the 1st through V20 Humanity system without the &quot;cheat&quot; of Paths or Roads.<br /> <br /> Really, the strangest thing about V5 is that it acts like the Lasombra of the Dark Ages continued largely unchanged from the 12th century to the 20th. I don't believe the Lasombra would, for example, have much interest in modern religion or the Catholic Church after the Sabbat but it acts like they never lost their influence or trends toward such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T10:25:00-08:00","id":1498970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498967#post1498967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I feel like this pretty much makes a lot of assumptions about V5 as a playstyle that doesn't seem to be backed up by many of the supplements. V5 goes very hard on the idea that vampires are scumbags and there's not much point in trying to be a &quot;good&quot; one. Instead, it goes with the idea vampires should have SOME redeeming qualities but you are overall an evil person and a psychopath.<br /> <br /> The Humanity system, when done right can be overall extremely alien and vile depending on the Chronicle Tenets and your personal code of ethics.<br /> <br /> Certainly, it allows a lot more flexibility than the 1st through V20 Humanity system without the &quot;cheat&quot; of Paths or Roads.<br /> <br /> Really, the strangest thing about V5 is that it acts like the Lasombra of the Dark Ages continued largely unchanged from the 12th century to the 20th. I don't believe the Lasombra would, for example, have much interest in modern religion or the Catholic Church after the Sabbat but it acts like they never lost their influence or trends toward such.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also leans into the idea of vampirism as an unbearable curse and a soarce of endless woe.<br /> <br /> Yeah it ls possible to engineer v5 to something truly vile but that isn't really in spirit with v5s intent and will get tricky with stuff like touchstones and author intent.<br /> <br /> Roads and paths arnt a cheat so no it doesn't.<br /> <br /> That's certainly true i agree, v5 seems to try and reset the clan to dark age as the 'true' clan. Without considering that's an period aspect of the clan rather than the norm. It'd be like insisting the v5 ventrue march around in full plate. Shadow brokers and sinister priests are aspects of the clan not the whole clan, prior to v5 for every little finger their was a tywin, a palpatine and a Walter white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-07-2022, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T11:38:18-08:00","id":1498978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498875#post1498875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean some people think wizard and sorcerer mean the exact same thing without any different connotations and thus it's entirely possible that &quot;mystics&quot; was an arbitrary choice?<br /> Unlikely. Literally every other pre-v5 magical group in VTM has picked appropriate names for themselves, it'd be weird if Mystics was an arbitration. The only stickler is maybe &quot;necromancer&quot; if we go by strict &quot;What the latin means&quot; conventions and even then, half the more common necromancy powers fit within that definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that if a group or a particular person goes by social conventions or norms, or by mundane details or straightforward / simple practicalities, then it is possible - though maybe highly unlikely, depending on the role or the kind / type of persron that needs a titlte, a term, a definition, or a name - that a different word will be chosen rather then the one that seems to fit in regard to the function of a particular role or the ideas of a particular group. Such a choice would not be arbitrary in my opinion, as there are stil some definite criteria.<br /> In fact it could be said that the criteria used in regard to choice of a word, term, or a name are social or grounded in emotions, rather than intellectual or grounded in knowledge. But in such a situations the choice of a particular name or a word could definitely seem quite / rather arbitrary to at least some extent.<br /> <br /> Why exactly did you mention the word (or title) &quot;necromancer&quot; as an exception? Is this because a similar or comparable word in Latin is related to knowledge, scrying, divining, and comprehension in regard to wraiths, spectral undead, and ghosts?<br /> <br /> How are you certain that every pre-V5 spellcasting / sorcery group in Vampire: the Masquerade (and what about the wider World of Darkness?) has picked appropriate and correct words and terms in regard to their titles and roles? I would say that maybe some of them were at least to a slight - but perhaps significant - extent influenced by emotional or social criteria in regard to such choices and decisions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T07:36:01-08:00","id":1499061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1498970#post1498970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also leans into the idea of vampirism as an unbearable curse and a soarce of endless woe.<br /> <br /> Yeah it ls possible to engineer v5 to something truly vile but that isn't really in spirit with v5s intent and will get tricky with stuff like touchstones and author intent.<br /> <br /> Roads and paths arnt a cheat so no it doesn't.<br /> <br /> That's certainly true i agree, v5 seems to try and reset the clan to dark age as the 'true' clan. Without considering that's an period aspect of the clan rather than the norm. It'd be like insisting the v5 ventrue march around in full plate. Shadow brokers and sinister priests are aspects of the clan not the whole clan, prior to v5 for every little finger their was a tywin, a palpatine and a Walter white.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 suffers from a number of urban myths: that you are forced to play a positive character bemoaning the vampiric condition is the most common!<br /> <br /> Author intent, as Charles has underlined, is very much to say &quot;Vampires are vile creatures that taint everything they touch&quot;: you can play a perfectly evil character, either by tailoring the Chronicle tenets, or by creating relevant Convinctions that can easily represent Paths, as it is suggested in the Corebook and in Cults of the Blood Gods).<br /> <br /> Even the fact that Convinctions are tied to Human Touchstones is not necessarily limiting: those Humans must remind you of your values, it's not required you love them or that you have a positive relationship with them.<br /> <br /> An evil backstabbing Lasombra politician might groom a human puppet without any moral qualm, a murderous Frank Underwood who will absolutely do every shit to get it to the top, and use it as the Touchstone for his &quot;Only the Fittest Survive&quot; touchstone.<br /> <br /> A sociopathic Lasombra nihilist on the Path of Night equivalent might have as Touchstones his favoured victims, whose continued misery remind him of his Convinction &quot;No rest for the wicked&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't you be able to play Palpatine, Tywin and Walter White? Looking at Clan stereotypes in the Chicago book, they are very much in line with these kind of archetypes.<br /> <br /> I think, btw, that Revised Lasombra suffered from a lack of focus: they are a clan of social darwinists, but also of nihilists, but also of powers behind the throne and manipulators, that are into Church culture (organization, social mobility, hierarchy) but also piracy (extrem anarchy, unchecked competition) but also old style limpieza de sangre aristocracy (extreme conservatism and racial hierarchies) ... Lots of cool concepts, but perhaps a bit too many for a single clan, and not one of the biggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 12-07-2022, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T07:43:16-08:00","id":1499062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499061#post1499061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> V5 suffers from a number of urban myths: that you are forced to play a positive character bemoaning the vampiric condition is the most common!<br /> <br /> Author intent, as Charles has underlined, is very much to say &quot;Vampires are vile creatures that taint everything they touch&quot;: you can play a perfectly evil character, either by tailoring the Chronicle tenets, or by creating relevant Convinctions that can easily represent Paths, as it is suggested in the Corebook and in Cults of the Blood Gods).<br /> <br /> Even the fact that Convinctions are tied to Human Touchstones is not necessarily limiting: those Humans must remind you of your values, it's not required you love them or that you have a positive relationship with them.<br /> <br /> An evil backstabbing Lasombra politician might groom a human puppet without any moral qualm, a murderous Frank Underwood who will absolutely do every shit to get it to the top, and use it as the Touchstone for his &quot;Only the Fittest Survive&quot; touchstone. <br /> <br /> A sociopathic Lasombra nihilist on the Path of Night equivalent might have as Touchstones his favoured victims, whose continued misery remind him of his Convinction &quot;No rest for the wicked&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't you be able to play Palpatine, Tywin and Walter White? Looking at Clan stereotypes in the Chicago book, they are very much in line with these kind of archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These arnt urban myths, these are guesstimates from different interpretations, statements releases and the mechanics.<br /> <br /> As presented in v5 vampires are vile but in a downward spiral crackhead way, if author intent was otherwise theyve failed. You can certainly do those things but you're really stretching the game to breaking point in the attempt. Co dependant abusive dynamics are neither how Touchstones are presented nor how lasombra approach kine.<br /> <br /> Path of night is explicitly discouraged, like all paths. You'd barely be aware of its existence at all unless you read outside of edition.<br /> <br /> In answer to your question Because you'll wassail in about a week unless the gm is really nice.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind I'm not saying it can't be done (given about 20 minutes I could probably knock up mechanics to play a groomer baali on revelations) I'm saying it doesn't synergise well with the games design or execution. Yes I could play a palpatine but it wouldn't work very well as presented, would require heavy negotiation from other players, a gm with lax views on Touchstone interactions and probably still be a bit crap. You're not playing to the games strengths and that's why lasombra don't really work in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-08-2022, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T21:24:31-08:00","id":1499119,"title":"","content":"You have things like creating ghouls and childer always gives stains regardless of chronicle tenets. This heavily implies that they only intend tenets to be within a certain range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T23:04:33-08:00","id":1499126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499119#post1499119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have things like creating ghouls and childer always gives stains regardless of chronicle tenets. This heavily implies that they only intend tenets to be within a certain range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even think that's the case. I just think it's badly written.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T03:10:14-08:00","id":1499204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499126#post1499126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't even think that's the case. I just think it's badly written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most everybody can agree that V5 probably needed an extra year of kit-bashing and playtest before publication to get the rules to deliver whatever kind of experience the developers meant.<br /> <br /> There are some concepts there, but all too many things seem either too unfinished and raw or unclear on objective due to a kind of scattershot presentation. At least my humble and admitedly half-baked opinion from previous attempts at trying to navigate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T12:56:56-08:00","id":1499239,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1444431]The thread for discussing all things Keeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla<br /> <br /> I'm not bothered that a number of older Keepers have defected to join the Camarilla as they saw how that there greatest achievement of destroying there antidulivan was an abject failure and lost the will to continue the &quot;fight&quot; and go back to the shadowy manipulators they were in the Dark Ages. I'm sure some of them miss the good old days of competiting with the Ventrue for influence with style and grace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T13:11:28-08:00","id":1499240,"title":"","content":"My main objection is it contributes nothing to the setting, makes the lasombra look weak, discredits them conceptually and is badly written. You may as well had the ventrue implode the carmarilla and join the Sabbat because them riding around with a broadsword on a ghouled horse is the 'true' clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-09-2022, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T14:41:22-08:00","id":1499249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499240#post1499240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main objection is it contributes nothing to the setting, makes the lasombra look weak, discredits them conceptually and is badly written. You may as well had the ventrue implode the carmarilla and join the Sabbat because them riding around with a broadsword on a ghouled horse is the 'true' clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is a matter of opinion because the Sabbat is objectively less successful than the Camarilla and being in charge of the Sabbat doesn't actually make the Lasombra look great.<br /> <br /> Mind you, a lot of fans try to re-envision the Sabbat as something OTHER than 80% Soccer Hooligans and pretty much ignore that it is, canonically, 80% Soccer Hooligans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T15:38:11-08:00","id":1499255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499249#post1499249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel this is a matter of opinion because the Sabbat is objectively less successful than the Camarilla and being in charge of the Sabbat doesn't actually make the Lasombra look great.<br /> <br /> Mind you, a lot of fans try to re-envision the Sabbat as something OTHER than 80% Soccer Hooligans and pretty much ignore that it is, canonically, 80% Soccer Hooligans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything is a matter of opinion in fiction or art. Somebody somewhere thinks godfather is a terrible movie. It doesn't make them look great in the same sense running the carmarilla doesn't make the ventrue look great or running the anarchs makes the brujah look great. The sabbats success prior to v5 is comparitable to the carmarilla in terms of territory and praxis to the point the faction was a credible threat to the ivory tower. That's like saying the sassanid empire was garbage because it wasn't as succesful as Rome.<br /> <br /> You're drastically overstating your case with the football yob metaphor. Not in the least because anarchs are a lot closer to football yobs if you're remotely familiar with how such groups operate. Their isn't really an irl equivelant to the Sabbat, partly because its a political group which exists outside of human social and economic theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-10-2022, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T11:33:55-08:00","id":1499300,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> The remaining Lasombra back in the Sabbat<br /> <br /> I'm mostly unconcerned with the few remaining Keepers left in the Sabbat as they have lost most of there capable leadership to either the Camarilla or the Anarchs to a lesser degree in our game and that the sect is for all intents and purposes gone with a few roving die hard packs that are slowly but surely being elminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T12:25:24-08:00","id":1499305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499300#post1499300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The remaining Lasombra back in the Sabbat<br /> <br /> I'm mostly unconcerned with the few remaining Keepers left in the Sabbat as they have lost most of there capable leadership to either the Camarilla or the Anarchs to a lesser degree in our game and that the sect is for all intents and purposes gone with a few roving die hard packs that are slowly but surely being elminated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically speaking Sabbat lasombra have better long terms prospects than the defectors due to differences in sect embracing policies<br /> Carmarilla lasombra are roughly 8th maybe 9th in line for embracing rights in a period where the sect is keeping its numbers low. Not to mention the casualty rates amoung defectors would have be brutal. I think more likely the carmarilla lasombra are the dead men walking. On reflection the writters are effectively going to have to ignore the ramifications of the current setting moving forward since the lasombra should be considered a bloodline and complete joke in v5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-10-2022, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T13:26:03-08:00","id":1499308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499305#post1499305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logically speaking Sabbat lasombra have better long terms prospects than the defectors due to differences in sect embracing policies<br /> Carmarilla lasombra are roughly 8th maybe 9th in line for embracing rights in a period where the sect is keeping its numbers low. Not to mention the casualty rates amoung defectors would have be brutal. I think more likely the carmarilla lasombra are the dead men walking. On reflection the writters are effectively going to have to ignore the ramifications of the current setting moving forward since the lasombra should be considered a bloodline and complete joke in v5</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a couple of points here that need to be addressed:<br /> <br /> 1.<b> The Sabbat have really taken a beating in V5 as not just a sect but as a concept:</b> Paradox has decided the Sabbat are something they flat out either do not like or do not want to particularly see succeed as a playstyle. As such, they've decided to take the Sabbat Civil War of BJD and the &quot;Gehenna War&quot; to destroy the sect. As the Sabbat are my second favorite group after the Anarchs (who the Sabbat are the poor cousins of the aweseomeness thereof), this is somethin I don't like.<br /> <br /> However, they have REALLY gone to town on making the Sabbat collapse into parodies of themselves. I don't like it. It's not something I appreciate but they have been hammering the Sabbat collapsing for the better part of five years now.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra defection<br /> * The Tzimisce defections<br /> * The destruction of some of its most popular Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> * Defections to Blood Cults<br /> * Massive casualties due to the Gehenna War(s)<br /> * Loss of territory<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> I don't know who has a bee in their bonnett (forgive my Southernism) about the Sword of Caine but the Sabbat really is wrecked beyond all repair. Barring a new edition, those who have fled this sinking ship seem the best off.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Some people have collective amnesia about the Lasombra Antitribu: </b>I mentioned this above and I think people are pretending that it wasn't the case in V1,2,Revised,20 because they're so pissed off about 1#. Believe me, I get that because I find the treatment of the Sabbat in 1# to be ridiculous. It's my 2nd biggest complaint about the game and frankly, might be my biggest.<br /> <br /> However, the Lasombra Antitribu have always been the most powerful Bloodline in the Camarilla and always JUST SHORT of having their own seat on the Inner Council. They have a 4th generation Methuselah in the inner circles of the Camarilla after all, which is arguably more powerful than all of the other Inner Council combined.<br /> <br /> The idea the Lasombra need THAT many defections to go from being a bloodline to a full Clan in the Camarilla is a stretch. Remember, there were Lasombra Princes in the previous city and not just Marcus Vitel. Really, the biggest weirdness about the &quot;defection&quot; is acting like the Lasombra didn't ALWAYS have a steady line of defectors from the Sabbat. They weren't exactly A LOT of them and plenty did get tracked down and killed but they weren't ever unheard of either. An entire city once defected.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>I get the impression Justin Achilli doesn't have complete freedom here</b>: The Sabbat depicted in The Sword of Caine are a swarm of zombies and make the previous Revised take on the Sabbat look positively enlightened. However, if you talk with Justin Achilli on Twitter or other social media, he says that the modern Sabbat are just a cover for the Elders who are sitting in their bunkers sending them all out to die.<br /> <br /> That the &quot;true Sabbat&quot; is tsill around, just waiting Gehenna out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&a