ouncil. They have a 4th generation Methuselah in the inner circles of the Camarilla after all, which is arguably more powerful than all of the other Inner Council combined.<br /> <br /> The idea the Lasombra need THAT many defections to go from being a bloodline to a full Clan in the Camarilla is a stretch. Remember, there were Lasombra Princes in the previous city and not just Marcus Vitel. Really, the biggest weirdness about the &quot;defection&quot; is acting like the Lasombra didn't ALWAYS have a steady line of defectors from the Sabbat. They weren't exactly A LOT of them and plenty did get tracked down and killed but they weren't ever unheard of either. An entire city once defected.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>I get the impression Justin Achilli doesn't have complete freedom here</b>: The Sabbat depicted in The Sword of Caine are a swarm of zombies and make the previous Revised take on the Sabbat look positively enlightened. However, if you talk with Justin Achilli on Twitter or other social media, he says that the modern Sabbat are just a cover for the Elders who are sitting in their bunkers sending them all out to die.<br /> <br /> That the &quot;true Sabbat&quot; is tsill around, just waiting Gehenna out.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) probably, but they could just as easily soft retcon the sabbat back to power anytime they feel like. V5 is full of them anyway. I mean the Sabbat book subtly contradicts itself anyway.<br /> <br /> 2) the lasombra antitribu were in pretty small numbers and this was something of a plot point. <br /> <br /> 3) hard to say, were working off guesswork here.<br /> <br /> Its probably worth noting 1 and 3 wouldn't really change the lasombra being a borderline bloodline and 2 is pretty weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-10-2022, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://fo