.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T14:45:58-08:00","id":1499316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499314#post1499314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh:<br /> <br /> They were a Bloodline not a Clan in the Camarilla but they were probably the largest Bloodline. Given there's only about 2000 vampires of each Clan with 1:100000 numbers, there's not that much difference,</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the largest bloodline in the camarilla isnt an achievement. Theirs what? The gargoyles? The seven on the sneak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-10-2022, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T15:00:38-08:00","id":1499317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499314#post1499314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given there's only about 2000 vampires of each Clan with 1:100000 numbers, there's not that much difference,</div> </div> </div> </div>The clans are not equivalent in population. We know there is a big difference between the more populous clans and the least populous ones.<br /> <br /> We know the Brujah are by far the largest clan period with their promiscuous embraces and outlawry. When you combine them with the brothers among the Anarchs and Sabbat, they are probably the largest clan of vampires in the world.<br /> <br /> I would say the Gangrel, Toreador, and Ventrue fall in the next spot. They were fairly dominant members of the Camarilla. The Gangrel were not as well represented in the cities, but had a substantial number in the outlands and the wilderness.<br /> <br /> I would say the Nosferatu probably have noticeably less numbers than the last three, but would still appear substantial.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians and Tremere probably had the lowest numbers of the classic seven clans for different reasons. <br /> <br /> I am sure others have different ideas in mind, but this is what I use as general numbers although individual domains can have very different ratios.<br /> <br /> Anyone else would be less than these, including the Lasombra anti-tribu. Obviously rare bloodlines like the Daughters of Cacophony and Samedi would be less. But would they have a higher population than Caitiff? In almost every case the Lasombra anti-tribu are mentioned, it states that they are limited in the number of domains they are in, generally around the Mediterranean, and they sometimes get mentioned in South America. They seem very restricted in the domains they are in.<br /> <br /> Yes, Montano was very old and powerful, but it's not like the Camarilla was lacking in numbers of incredibly ancient and powerful vampires. Plus given his age, it was never quite sure how active he was in modern nights or whether he went through long periods of torpor. Like anything when a detailed history is not given, every ST fills in the blanks according to what they like.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is much evidence that the Lasombra anti-tribu were so large that they were somehow almost a peer of the classic seven. We are not given any information to think that in any of the sourcebooks that I know of. That sounds more like something an individual ST wants to house rule. As many fans like the Lasombra anti-tribu, it is only natural that they want to see them increase in number and become more ubiquitous. And that's fine, but it was not canon. If the Lasombra truly were as large as the classic seven clans, then it would have been much more likely they would have given them membership on the Inner Circle originally, buth they didn't so they weren't.<br /> <br /> Of course, as I often mention we have many different versions of canon now as the idea that there is one continuity between the different versions of the game are becoming increasingly unrealistic. The 1e/2e, Revised, V20, and V5 are pretty much their own worlds using the same concepts but making lots of changes that create incompatible versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T00:28:28-08:00","id":1499352,"title":"","content":"I always thought they missed the forest for the trees with carmarilla lasombra when they ignored the ashirra. It would have been much each to write in a surge in numbers from the middle east with recent developments rather than the comedy of errors they presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T08:08:55-08:00","id":1499375,"title":"","content":"-The seven clans are of course going to be more populous than the other six because they're generalists with broadly applicable skills/disciplines and thus they can spread more effectively than specialists like the other six clans or the bloodlines who are really all about embracing from a very narrow selection of people and getting into niche markets (and tend to form sects of their own) <br /> <br /> -The Ashirra have outlived their usefulness (putting the Baali/Assamites in check) and really now only serve to <i>other </i>the muslim world. That they still exist is the product of liberal whites fetishizing the east/minorities and/or corporate virtue signalling. I'd much rather just have the Cam be the global conspiracy it was originally intended to be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> questioning whether the Lasombra actually should belong to the sabbat when it's so against their values </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you can actually read the books and have this opinion. There's a lot of players who don't read the books and just trust that whatever is going on in their game is as-canon intended; that's the only circumstance where I can imagine a reasonable person would reason that Lasombra had been misplaced in their majority sect choice. They are perfect for the Sabbat. For the Camarilla, they're passable, but undesirable; natural brutes, authoritarians, power hungry control freaks and religious devotees are <i>not</i> what the camarilla is after. <br /> <br /> Just looking at who-plays what clans without reading the books will make you terribly misinformed. You'd start to think the Tremere are clowns, that the Gangrel and Brujah could only ever be autuark murder-hobos and don't belong in the Camarilla at all, That Malkavians are a joke clan, that settites radiate sleaze and that all Ventrue are cartoonish bourgeoise assholes who don't know how to talk to common people but insist that you have to put up with their bullshit because they &quot;Have 4's in Charisma/Manipulation/Appearance&quot;. <br /> The setting should not be dictated by how it is commonly (mis)played, but by reason. That goes more than triple for LARP: You're all welcome to your own fun but the idea that well written art can take a dumpster dive because some adults were playing dress up and were using rock, paper scissors to decide if they could stay invisible and not get detected by the guy they were playing RPS with. Good movies have good writing and good casting and professional acting and <i>plenty of retakes</i>. I refuse to have concessions made for LARP impact tabletop rules, and I refuse to have LARP, one of the most limited mediums there is, influence metaplot for a game that primarily isn't LARP. IDGAFF that Lasombra are popular in LARP. If what I'm told is true and we go by LARP, the Sabbat should always win except for the last bit where the game master decides the Camarilla needs to win. <br /> <br /> <br /> Right, that's enough spice for one post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T09:37:34-08:00","id":1499385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499375#post1499375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ashirra have outlived their usefulness (putting the Baali/Assamites in check) and really now only serve to other the muslim world. That they still exist is the product of liberal whites fetishizing the east/minorities and/or corporate virtue signalling. I'd much rather just have the Cam be the global conspiracy it was originally intended to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears V5 agrees with you and that's the purpose of combining them in the Modern World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the Camarilla, they're passable, but undesirable; natural brutes, authoritarians, power hungry control freaks and religious devotees are <i>not</i> what the camarilla is after. </div> </div> </div>I always found the idea of Revised that the Camarilla would outlaw the Caine myth to be ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-11-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T10:06:42-08:00","id":1499387,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure how the Lasombra could be updated in the new edition outside of new characters or updated lore on existing characters like Talley, Lucita, Montano or Mariam Bint Ashiha, I would like to see more Lasombra clan lore sheets. Such descendants of the more famous Keepers like Montano and his fellow \u201csiblings \u201c and what kind of benefits you would get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T10:14:24-08:00","id":1499390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499385#post1499385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always found the idea of Revised that the Camarilla would outlaw the Caine myth to be ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Strictly speaking they outlawed Caine worship and 3rd gen conspiracy theories. Which considering their absurd conduct in 5th was probably a good idea. Praying at methusulahs isn't just immoral its moronic. I'm not even convinced accepting Caine worship is a good idea since it makes Sabbat infiltration and subversion way easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-11-2022, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T10:17:29-08:00","id":1499391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499385#post1499385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found the idea of Revised that the Camarilla would outlaw the Caine myth to be ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's ridiculous. <br /> 1: I don't think the inner circle would have that much power. <br /> 2: I think it makes a good amount of political sense to clamp down on Gehenna cults. But &quot;Vampire FSB appears every time someone humours the idea of a biblical murderer&quot; would surely encourage conspiratorial thinking. Rational discussion and casual disdain would do wonders in bringing about disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T16:40:30-08:00","id":1499409,"title":"","content":"Considering that humans have a hard time with rational thinking. Why would former humans be any different in that regard is my question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T22:25:22-08:00","id":1499420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499409#post1499409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that humans have a hard time with rational thinking. Why would former humans be any different in that regard is my question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have a strong tendency to embrace above-average people, combine that with the selection pressures of unlife (not meeting the sun, not killing yourself, not breaking the law and getting killed, not getting murdered) and yeah, it's pretty reasonable to assume that the overwhelming majority would favour reason. That and people who aren't that smart will likely just follow the herd/whatever the sire says. Peer pressure is not to be underestimated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-12-2022, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T22:28:36-08:00","id":1499421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499420#post1499420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have a strong tendency to embrace above-average people, combine that with the selection pressures of unlife (not meeting the sun, not killing yourself, not breaking the law and getting killed, not getting murdered) and yeah, it's pretty reasonable to assume that the overwhelming majority would favour reason. That and people who aren't that smart will likely just follow the herd/whatever the sire says.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I'd say intelligence isn't the best determinator for surviving as a vampire. It's more moral flexibility. Not too psychotic to become a wight. Not too moral to be unable to deal with being a predatory monster.<br /> <br /> Intelligence is certainly beneficial but a good chunk of the Clans value other qualities over it: Gangrel (Survival, Physical Prowess), Brujah (Physical Prowess, Charisma), Malkavians (very deeply irrational thinking), Toreador (Charisma, Talent, Beauty), and Nosferatu (Rationality is more or less taught by the school of hard knocks post-Embrace).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-12-2022, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T00:38:51-08:00","id":1499423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499420#post1499420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have a strong tendency to embrace above-average people, combine that with the selection pressures of unlife (not meeting the sun, not killing yourself, not breaking the law and getting killed, not getting murdered) and yeah, it's pretty reasonable to assume that the overwhelming majority would favour reason. That and people who aren't that smart will likely just follow the herd/whatever the sire says. Peer pressure is not to be underestimated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are highly functioning schizophrenics with a violent drug addiction, I wouldn't over-estimate their attitude for rational thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T01:33:30-08:00","id":1499425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499423#post1499423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are highly functioning schizophrenics with a violent drug addiction, I wouldn't over-estimate their attitude for rational thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not every Clan is the Tremere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T09:20:27-08:00","id":1499447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499421#post1499421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, I'd say intelligence isn't the best determinator for surviving as a vampire. It's more moral flexibility. Not too psychotic to become a wight. Not too moral to be unable to deal with being a predatory monster.<br /> <br /> Intelligence is certainly beneficial but a good chunk of the Clans value other qualities over it: Gangrel (Survival, Physical Prowess), Brujah (Physical Prowess, Charisma), Malkavians (very deeply irrational thinking), Toreador (Charisma, Talent, Beauty), and Nosferatu (Rationality is more or less taught by the school of hard knocks post-Embrace).</div> </div> </div> </div>What qualities would you give to the Ventrue, the Tzimisce, the Lasombra, or to the Followers of Set [ Or Setites, or otherwise Ministers. ] and the other Independent Clans?<br /> <br /> The Gangrel (Vampires and also most likely Gangrel Ghouls) definitely value freedom and respect to a considerable extent.<br /> <br /> For the Malkavians imagination, humour, and the community are key and meaningful.<br /> <br /> The Warlocks [ The title \\ nickname \\ moniker for the Tremere Antitribu Vampiresses and Vampires is Spellbinders, by the way. ] place obligations, loyalty, and trust rather highly, and also value them to a significant degree \\ extent.<br /> <br /> The Toreador Vampires (And to some extent also woman and man who are Toreador Ghouls, as well.) are known, respected, and liked for their interest in personal expression, pride, hedonism, pleasure, enjoyment, and entertainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-12-2022, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T10:30:26-08:00","id":1499453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499447#post1499447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What qualities would you give to the Ventrue, the Tzimisce, the Lasombra, or to the Followers of Set [ Or Setites, or otherwise Ministers. ] and the other Independent Clans?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're spraking in generalities rather than specifics because any Embraces by a vampire of Clan X is going to be determined by other factors than the Clan &quot;type.&quot; These will include what the vampire needs at the moment (&quot;I need a rich asshole to fund my latest scheme&quot;, &quot;I need a guy to serve as a bodyguard&quot;, and &quot;I need someone to feed off of because I have the Methuselah's Thirst.&quot;) Plus any of their personal biases (&quot;I don't embrace poor people&quot;, &quot;I don't embrace white people&quot;, &quot;I don't embrace non-Christians&quot;).<br /> <br /> However, if I were to give some minor thoughts:<br /> <br /> * Ventrue: Ventrue, like the Tremere do like to Embrace rational types. However, more than rationality, they prefer to have cultured breeding and socially upward attitudes. Wealth is also something they're rather crassly focused on Pre-Embrace as well.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Charisma, Intelligence, Resources<br /> <br /> * Tzimisce: If we ignore shovelheads who either get with the program ot die, Tzimisce prefer embracing people who are educated, upper class, and detached. They will tend to go for doctors, lawyers, and people with some degree of clinical psychopathy if they can find it. Like the Tremere, they prefer rational people but their definition amounts to outsiders to social interaction but decisive managers. They'd prefer to Embrace someone who fires people for a living over someone who wins loyalty.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Low Humanity, Intelligence,<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra: The Lasombra prefer to Embrace people they view as impassioned and ruthless, which oddly makes them closer to the Brujah than the Ventrue or Tremere. Lasombra prefer a great deal more class but gravitate to schemers, criminals, and charismatic leaders. Politicians, people behind politicians, megachurch pastors, and psy-ops types. Rationality is less important than being able to manipulate others.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Manipulation, Charisma, Mid-to-Low Humanity<br /> <br /> * Followers of Set: The Followers of Set I'd argue look for two kinds of people. The first being someone who is utterly able to be rebuilt from the ground up and natural followers, the kind of people who join cults. The second are those people who are genuinely deeply religious with a mystical bent to their faiths. The latter are the ones they try to corrupt but not exactly destroy the faiths of because they want to repurpose it.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Charisma, Manipulation, fanaticism<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni: The Giovanni are always scheming to be Embraced so they actually usually are the people with the most constant focus on it. The easiest way to get Embraced is either occultism power or making a shitton of money. How you do the latter is less important and could be ponzi scheme or government contracts. Rationality is not really rewarded versus success and you could be a superstitious nutjob who consults horoscopes as long as it works.<br /> <br /> Attributes: Necromancy, Occult, Finance, Resources, Promixity to main bloodline<br /> <br /> * Ravnos: Depending on how you view them, the Ravnos generally favor the ability to trick others and charismatic personal relationships over other skills. A Ravnos is Embraced for their ability to survive by their wits and fast talk with a focus on non-violent crime as well as social interactions.<br /> <br /> Atributes: Wits, Charisma, Manipulation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-12-2022, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T11:40:34-08:00","id":1499772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444431-v5-the-lasombra-thread?p=1499423#post1499423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are highly functioning schizophrenics with a violent drug addiction, I wouldn't over-estimate their attitude for rational thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a good analogy about what it's like to be a Kindred in World Of Darkness and I should use it as a quote for my Malkavian researcher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}